1
00:00:01,140 --> 00:00:06,409
(This program contains indirect advertisements.)

2
00:00:06,410 --> 00:00:08,050
(Space Rice Cake)

3
00:00:08,510 --> 00:00:10,780
(Space Rice Cake)

4
00:00:11,850 --> 00:00:16,290
(They excitedly opened up for their 2nd day of business.)

5
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:18,260
(Space Rice Cake launched a new menu.)

6
00:00:18,490 --> 00:00:20,730
(Broccolino Basiliano)

7
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:22,960
(The vibrant light green color is an eye-catcher.)

8
00:00:23,090 --> 00:00:25,300
(It's called basil tteokbokki.)

9
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:29,200
(As soon as it launched, the praises poured in.)

10
00:00:29,970 --> 00:00:34,170
(They opened with full confidence and high spirits, but...)

11
00:00:36,370 --> 00:00:37,780
(Flustered)

12
00:00:38,110 --> 00:00:42,980
(They hit an unexpected snag with the hard rice cakes.)

13
00:00:43,620 --> 00:00:49,050
(And the customers kept on flooding in.)

14
00:00:49,350 --> 00:00:52,960
(Customers keep coming in slowly, just like Grand Prince Suyang.)

15
00:00:53,630 --> 00:00:57,600
(The crowd with the fierce vibe of Grand Prince Suyang want to order.)

16
00:00:57,830 --> 00:00:59,930
(Yu Jin comes right away.)

17
00:01:00,300 --> 00:01:01,499
Take your time with the menu and feel free to ask me...

18
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:02,869
- Jade Emperor Tteokbokki...
- Yes.

19
00:01:02,870 --> 00:01:04,440
Please feel free to ask me anything.

20
00:01:04,940 --> 00:01:07,210
Two of that and one pomegranate slushy, please.

21
00:01:07,310 --> 00:01:09,269
- Would you like any soda with that?
- No.

22
00:01:09,270 --> 00:01:11,610
Okay. Got it.

23
00:01:12,010 --> 00:01:13,509
One pomegranate slushy...

24
00:01:13,510 --> 00:01:14,779
- and one tteokramisu chestnut, yes?
- Yes.

25
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:15,949
- Coming right up.
- Thank you.

26
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:16,979
Thank you.

27
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:18,919
- If you like mala tteokbokki, - Yes.

28
00:01:18,920 --> 00:01:20,520
- I totally recommend it. Yes.
- Really?

29
00:01:20,990 --> 00:01:22,119
- We got orders.
- Okay.

30
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:23,296
All right. Hit us with the orders.

31
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:25,559
(Tteokbokki Order Status: two small original tteokbokki, )

32
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:27,790
(one small basil tteokbokki, one small mala tteokbokki)

33
00:01:27,960 --> 00:01:29,059
One small basil tteokbokki.

34
00:01:29,060 --> 00:01:30,129
(It's a bolt out of the blue.)

35
00:01:30,130 --> 00:01:31,629
- Coming right up.
- Okay.

36
00:01:31,630 --> 00:01:33,769
Look at this green onion that Yu Jin chopped.

37
00:01:33,770 --> 00:01:34,800
It's okay.

38
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:36,840
I didn't know Yu Jin was still here.

39
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:38,970
- I didn't give you something?
- No.

40
00:01:39,800 --> 00:01:41,009
- I'm sorry.
- Don't be.

41
00:01:41,010 --> 00:01:43,009
- Whatever it is, I'm sorry.
- I love you, Yu Jin.

42
00:01:43,010 --> 00:01:45,479
- That's okay.
- I just wanted to say I love you.

43
00:01:45,480 --> 00:01:46,480
I really love you.

44
00:01:46,481 --> 00:01:47,709
(She starts making tteokbokki before getting caught.)

45
00:01:47,710 --> 00:01:49,430
This is a bit too much of the sauce, but...

46
00:01:49,510 --> 00:01:51,180
Good. The rice cakes are in.

47
00:01:51,380 --> 00:01:53,180
Is today a special day or something?

48
00:01:54,420 --> 00:01:57,459
(Basil tteokbokki on the other side)

49
00:01:57,460 --> 00:01:59,459
- We'll be off.
- Yes. Thank you.

50
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:00,629
(Every single burner is fully ignited.)

51
00:02:00,630 --> 00:02:01,789
The rice cakes went in.

52
00:02:01,790 --> 00:02:03,129
(Tteokbokki Progress: Original and basil, in progress)

53
00:02:03,130 --> 00:02:06,630
(Mala, pending)

54
00:02:06,900 --> 00:02:08,869
- This cuts through the greasiness.
- It's good.

55
00:02:08,870 --> 00:02:10,870
(The customers outside are ready for dessert now.)

56
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:12,199
- It'll be ready shortly.
- Hold on.

57
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,609
(But there's still no sign of the desserts coming out.)

58
00:02:13,610 --> 00:02:14,610
Fishcakes.

59
00:02:14,970 --> 00:02:17,480
They didn't forget about our tteokramisu, right?

60
00:02:18,610 --> 00:02:19,980
Good. Thank you.

61
00:02:20,180 --> 00:02:21,550
I'm practicing.

62
00:02:21,880 --> 00:02:26,250
(She's a bit slow since it's her first time, but she's thorough.)

63
00:02:26,520 --> 00:02:28,890
(She looks more serious than ever since the grand opening.)

64
00:02:29,150 --> 00:02:30,960
(The next step is...)

65
00:02:31,890 --> 00:02:34,930
(to add a generous layer of chestnut powder.)

66
00:02:35,260 --> 00:02:38,360
(Eun Ji's first tteokramisu chestnut)

67
00:02:38,660 --> 00:02:44,200
(Like a squirrel storing acorns, she gathers the desserts.)

68
00:02:44,470 --> 00:02:48,310
(She keeps the spare desserts nice and cool in the fridge.)

69
00:02:48,740 --> 00:02:50,579
(Right after that, she serves the rest.)

70
00:02:50,580 --> 00:02:53,410
It's topped with a whole chestnut.

71
00:02:53,950 --> 00:02:54,950
That's right. Yes.

72
00:02:54,951 --> 00:02:56,556
(They take a big bite after waiting eagerly.)

73
00:02:56,580 --> 00:02:58,649
This is the perfect dessert after the spicy dish.

74
00:02:58,650 --> 00:02:59,650
Yes.

75
00:02:59,720 --> 00:03:00,750
It's good.

76
00:03:01,050 --> 00:03:02,550
The ocean breeze feels so great.

77
00:03:05,690 --> 00:03:08,060
(The ocean breeze blows by...)

78
00:03:08,430 --> 00:03:11,600
(to dry Young Ji's sweat...)

79
00:03:12,430 --> 00:03:14,700
(and cool down the heat.)

80
00:03:14,930 --> 00:03:17,100
I'm turning the heat up a little.

81
00:03:17,970 --> 00:03:19,340
This burner won't light.

82
00:03:20,470 --> 00:03:23,909
(The sky looks absolutely clear, )

83
00:03:23,910 --> 00:03:26,840
(but the weather in this area is...)

84
00:03:27,180 --> 00:03:28,409
(It's expected to stay sunny...)

85
00:03:28,410 --> 00:03:29,609
(from morning to afternoon, )

86
00:03:29,610 --> 00:03:31,219
(sitting right at 22°C...)

87
00:03:31,220 --> 00:03:32,656
(with a wind at the speed of 2.7m per second.)

88
00:03:32,680 --> 00:03:34,920
(It's a gentle breeze.)

89
00:03:35,690 --> 00:03:39,060
(But since we're near the ocean, the wind can be a lot stronger.)

90
00:03:39,660 --> 00:03:42,889
(That's it for today's weather forecast...)

91
00:03:42,890 --> 00:03:44,730
(Help me.)

92
00:03:45,030 --> 00:03:47,669
(Thanks to that wind, she's fighting a battle against nature.)

93
00:03:47,670 --> 00:03:49,876
Everytime I put it on low heat, the fire just blows out.

94
00:03:49,900 --> 00:03:50,940
Right.

95
00:03:51,370 --> 00:03:52,899
- That's what's happening right now.
- But I need to cook it on low heat.

96
00:03:52,900 --> 00:03:54,316
(The wind keeps blowing, leaving Young Ji flustered.)

97
00:03:54,340 --> 00:03:57,139
(The flame is flickering again.)

98
00:03:57,140 --> 00:03:58,910
(The fire blows out.)

99
00:03:59,840 --> 00:04:01,750
It went out again. This is annoying.

100
00:04:02,550 --> 00:04:04,980
- I've got this.
- You've got this.

101
00:04:06,250 --> 00:04:07,519
That happens.

102
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:08,749
(She's not angry.)

103
00:04:08,750 --> 00:04:10,289
(Tteokbokki Progress: Original, in progress, basil, fire out, )

104
00:04:10,290 --> 00:04:12,960
(mala, not even on the stove yet)

105
00:04:13,190 --> 00:04:15,750
(Thinking about the customers who are waiting for their food...)

106
00:04:15,930 --> 00:04:18,259
I've changed my strategy.

107
00:04:18,260 --> 00:04:19,476
(You must stay calm at times like this!)

108
00:04:19,500 --> 00:04:21,199
Please give me a moment.

109
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:22,929
Trust me.

110
00:04:22,930 --> 00:04:24,070
I trust you.

111
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:27,270
(She adjusts the heat with Chef Mimi's help.)

112
00:04:27,540 --> 00:04:28,969
The rice cakes look bouncy.

113
00:04:28,970 --> 00:04:30,169
(When the tteokbokki is simmered down to perfection...)

114
00:04:30,170 --> 00:04:32,209
- Thank you.
- They're hot. Be careful.

115
00:04:32,210 --> 00:04:34,150
- Got it.
- Be careful.

116
00:04:34,610 --> 00:04:36,780
- Small original tteokbokki is up.
- Okay.

117
00:04:37,780 --> 00:04:40,219
- Original tteokbokki is coming out.
- Okay.

118
00:04:40,220 --> 00:04:42,090
Another small original tteokbokki is ready.

119
00:04:42,520 --> 00:04:44,090
Basil tteokbokki is ready.

120
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:46,900
(Tteokbokki Progress: Mala, cooking starts now)

121
00:04:47,390 --> 00:04:49,950
It's my first time getting an order for a small portion of this.

122
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,460
(She puts rice cakes in the pot skillfully.)

123
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:58,200
(Then, she simmers it down.)

124
00:04:58,540 --> 00:05:00,409
- It's already too late.
- Why so busy today?

125
00:05:00,410 --> 00:05:01,669
(There's something missing here.)

126
00:05:01,670 --> 00:05:03,940
(She forgot beef loin again.)

127
00:05:04,310 --> 00:05:05,410
Oh, right. Okay.

128
00:05:05,780 --> 00:05:07,750
(But it's not okay without beef loin.)

129
00:05:08,210 --> 00:05:10,056
The mala tteokbokki will be ready in one minute.

130
00:05:10,080 --> 00:05:11,279
Young Ji, isn't mala tteokbokki supposed to...

131
00:05:11,280 --> 00:05:12,620
have beef loin?

132
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:16,490
(She's done for.)

133
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:19,990
(It's already simmered down. It's too late to cook beef loin.)

134
00:05:20,360 --> 00:05:22,759
(What do I do?)

135
00:05:22,760 --> 00:05:24,830
- Can you grill beef loin for me?
- Okay.

136
00:05:24,930 --> 00:05:26,399
(She boldly changes the recipe.)

137
00:05:26,400 --> 00:05:27,400
Thank you.

138
00:05:27,401 --> 00:05:29,430
(They get right into the plan.)

139
00:05:29,630 --> 00:05:30,769
(Sous Chef Duties: Pollack roe and clam pasta, fried sides, )

140
00:05:30,770 --> 00:05:32,840
(cheering up the head chef, grilling beef loin)

141
00:05:35,110 --> 00:05:36,269
(She puts beef loin in the frying pan.)

142
00:05:36,270 --> 00:05:39,309
A fistful of beef loin? It's okay.

143
00:05:39,310 --> 00:05:41,126
(While Mimi is stir-frying the meat quickly...)

144
00:05:41,150 --> 00:05:42,710
(Meanwhile, Young Ji...)

145
00:05:43,010 --> 00:05:45,950
(adds the rest of the toppings.)

146
00:05:46,180 --> 00:05:48,249
(Grand Prince Suyang solo table: Don't Eat Ghost Pepper Tteokbokki)

147
00:05:48,250 --> 00:05:50,250
(Lonely)

148
00:05:50,660 --> 00:05:53,260
- The tteokbokki will be ready soon.
- It's okay. Take your time.

149
00:05:53,490 --> 00:05:54,959
- She's waiting for mala tteokbokki.
- It's ready.

150
00:05:54,960 --> 00:05:56,389
- Oh, okay.
- It's ready.

151
00:05:56,390 --> 00:05:58,760
Just give me 20 seconds.

152
00:05:59,530 --> 00:06:02,100
(Finally, the beef loin is ready.)

153
00:06:02,970 --> 00:06:05,039
Stack it up nicely. Thank you.

154
00:06:05,040 --> 00:06:06,140
(Adding the toppings...)

155
00:06:06,400 --> 00:06:08,809
- Let's use this only for the meat.
- Mala tteokbokki is ready.

156
00:06:08,810 --> 00:06:10,010
Thank you for waiting.

157
00:06:10,110 --> 00:06:11,110
(Tteokbokki Progress: Original and basil, ready and served, )

158
00:06:11,111 --> 00:06:12,780
(mala, ready)

159
00:06:13,540 --> 00:06:16,550
Hello. I can take your payment here.

160
00:06:17,180 --> 00:06:19,749
- Thank you. Go home safely.
- Thank you. Bye.

161
00:06:19,750 --> 00:06:21,870
(The first customers from the opening time head out.)

162
00:06:22,120 --> 00:06:24,990
(The next wave of customers enters, leaving no tables empty.)

163
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:28,560
- Hello. I'm sorry for the wait.
- Hello.

164
00:06:28,990 --> 00:06:32,030
Oh, my. Yu Jin, the owner of the general store is here.

165
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:34,869
- My goodness. Welcome.
- Ma'am, you weren't there earlier.

166
00:06:34,870 --> 00:06:37,499
- You weren't there earlier.
- Will you give us more free food?

167
00:06:37,500 --> 00:06:38,899
The owner of the general store is here...

168
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:40,709
This is amazing. Please give me a second.

169
00:06:40,710 --> 00:06:42,750
(She quickly leaves to avoid an awkward situation.)

170
00:06:43,710 --> 00:06:45,409
- How many in your party?
- Four.

171
00:06:45,410 --> 00:06:46,840
Please give me a moment.

172
00:06:47,710 --> 00:06:48,879
Your table is ready inside.

173
00:06:48,880 --> 00:06:50,156
(Large parties are rolling in one after another.)

174
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:52,419
We've got 2 new parties of 4 and 5.

175
00:06:52,420 --> 00:06:54,650
- Let's see how it goes for now.
- Okay.

176
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:57,359
- Are you ready to order?
- Yes.

177
00:06:57,360 --> 00:06:58,360
- Hello.
- All right.

178
00:06:58,560 --> 00:07:00,259
Can we have one of everything?

179
00:07:00,260 --> 00:07:01,530
Please give me a second.

180
00:07:01,890 --> 00:07:03,660
(She's taken aback by these big eaters.)

181
00:07:03,900 --> 00:07:07,130
(Sensing the looming disaster, she gets her gear ready.)

182
00:07:07,530 --> 00:07:09,830
- Will you try the "Don't Eat" one?
- Yes.

183
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:12,470
Don't Eat Ghost Pepper Tteokbokki.

184
00:07:12,940 --> 00:07:15,940
- Don't Eat Ghost Pepper Tteokbokki.
- Yes.

185
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:17,540
Has anyone taken your order yet?

186
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:20,240
- May I take your order?
- Okay.

187
00:07:20,710 --> 00:07:23,779
Yes, please. We'd like to try something you recommend.

188
00:07:23,780 --> 00:07:25,620
- Then...
- If it's not good, we'll return it.

189
00:07:26,550 --> 00:07:29,519
- That won't happen. I'm confident.
- She sounds confident.

190
00:07:29,520 --> 00:07:32,660
I recommend one medium original tteokbokki...

191
00:07:32,760 --> 00:07:35,130
- We serve basil tteokbokki now.
- I see.

192
00:07:36,390 --> 00:07:38,300
Focus, everyone. We got another order.

193
00:07:39,800 --> 00:07:41,599
One small original tteokbokki,

194
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:43,369
one medium Don't Eat Ghost Pepper Tteokbokki,

195
00:07:43,370 --> 00:07:45,140
one medium pollack roe and clam pasta,

196
00:07:45,670 --> 00:07:48,639
one tteokramisu chestnut, one of each slushy,

197
00:07:48,640 --> 00:07:50,009
and one small Broccolino Basiliano.

198
00:07:50,010 --> 00:07:51,539
Wait. Can you repeat it just once?

199
00:07:51,540 --> 00:07:52,540
(Order Status: 2 original, 1 mala, 2 basil tteokbokki, )

200
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:53,540
(1 pasta, 1 tteokramisu chestnut, 2 slushies)

201
00:07:53,541 --> 00:07:56,250
(It's a lot.)

202
00:07:56,580 --> 00:07:59,650
(However...)

203
00:08:01,390 --> 00:08:02,620
Hello.

204
00:08:02,990 --> 00:08:04,690
Hello. Are there two in your party?

205
00:08:05,190 --> 00:08:07,330
Broccolino Basiliano...

206
00:08:07,660 --> 00:08:09,130
- One small portion.
- Yes.

207
00:08:09,530 --> 00:08:12,230
- We got an order. A new order.
- Thank you.

208
00:08:12,830 --> 00:08:14,300
A new order? No way.

209
00:08:15,270 --> 00:08:17,540
One medium original tteokbokki,

210
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,539
one medium Broccolino Basiliano,

211
00:08:20,540 --> 00:08:22,821
- and three pomegranate slushies.
- No way. You're lying.

212
00:08:22,870 --> 00:08:24,579
- Okay. Got it.
- Okay.

213
00:08:24,580 --> 00:08:26,979
(Tteokbokki Order Status: 2 original, 2 mala, 3 basil)

214
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:29,850
(She hasn't even started cooking a single one.)

215
00:08:30,580 --> 00:08:32,150
I'll change my cooking gloves.

216
00:08:32,880 --> 00:08:34,590
- Good attitude toward hygiene.
- Right.

217
00:08:35,090 --> 00:08:37,360
I keep getting the sauce on my hands.

218
00:08:38,260 --> 00:08:39,989
(Mimi scans the kitchen with the eye of a hawk.)

219
00:08:39,990 --> 00:08:43,060
I want to check if people like my tteokbokki.

220
00:08:43,760 --> 00:08:45,030
They're all cold now.

221
00:08:45,860 --> 00:08:48,270
One, two, three. One, two, three, four, five.

222
00:08:49,130 --> 00:08:52,040
(After lining up the fried food, )

223
00:08:52,240 --> 00:08:54,310
(she starts cooking pollack roe and clam pasta.)

224
00:08:54,640 --> 00:08:58,280
I guess we're dealing with two large parties right now.

225
00:08:58,910 --> 00:09:01,050
(The special sauce for original tteokbokki)

226
00:09:01,710 --> 00:09:04,780
(Chili bean sauce and Sichuan pepper oil for mala tteokbokki)

227
00:09:05,180 --> 00:09:07,990
(Making the base for basil tteokbokki)

228
00:09:08,620 --> 00:09:10,920
(The three-pot system is on.)

229
00:09:11,460 --> 00:09:12,619
(But...)

230
00:09:12,620 --> 00:09:14,420
The burner with the mala tteokbokki went out.

231
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:16,560
Okay.

232
00:09:16,561 --> 00:09:17,930
(The burner is acting up again.)

233
00:09:18,130 --> 00:09:19,450
It's doing this to me on purpose.

234
00:09:19,760 --> 00:09:21,270
It wants me to go through ordeals.

235
00:09:23,200 --> 00:09:27,410
(Young Ji's Ordeal 1: The delayed wait time)

236
00:09:27,810 --> 00:09:29,610
I'm way too experienced for this.

237
00:09:29,910 --> 00:09:32,279
Oh, we're out of sausages.

238
00:09:32,280 --> 00:09:33,509
Gosh, my back hurts.

239
00:09:33,510 --> 00:09:34,956
(Young Ji's Ordeal 2: Running out of ingredients)

240
00:09:34,980 --> 00:09:36,380
What's going on? What's the matter?

241
00:09:37,250 --> 00:09:39,019
(Young Ji's Ordeal 3: Hard rice cakes)

242
00:09:39,020 --> 00:09:40,480
Calm down.

243
00:09:40,950 --> 00:09:43,990
- Calm down. It's okay.
- Calm down.

244
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:46,660
(And here's our dear sous chef.)

245
00:09:47,220 --> 00:09:48,490
Where is my thermometer?

246
00:09:49,430 --> 00:09:52,330
(Believe it or not, Mimi mixes English with Korean when flustered.)

247
00:09:52,530 --> 00:09:55,070
(While the kitchen is in chaos...)

248
00:09:55,930 --> 00:09:58,100
(The table is empty.)

249
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,410
(She drinks dongchimi while waiting for the food.)

250
00:10:02,170 --> 00:10:04,110
Are they making rice cakes to make the dishes?

251
00:10:04,980 --> 00:10:08,480
(We do make our own rice cakes, but we're not doing it right now.)

252
00:10:08,750 --> 00:10:11,520
(The kitchen still needs more time.)

253
00:10:11,720 --> 00:10:13,250
(What they need right now is...)

254
00:10:13,480 --> 00:10:14,849
I'm sorry for the delay.

255
00:10:14,850 --> 00:10:16,319
- It'll take just a bit longer, - That's okay.

256
00:10:16,320 --> 00:10:17,819
So we prepared these for you. They're on the house.

257
00:10:17,820 --> 00:10:19,689
- They're coffee slushies. Try them.
- Thanks.

258
00:10:19,690 --> 00:10:21,760
- Hello?
- Please wait just a bit longer.

259
00:10:22,290 --> 00:10:25,059
The owner of the general store is here, but I've been way too busy...

260
00:10:25,060 --> 00:10:27,730
with customers to properly take care of you. I'm sorry.

261
00:10:27,830 --> 00:10:30,499
- Come on. Don't be like this.
- I'm sorry I didn't recognize you.

262
00:10:30,500 --> 00:10:32,069
- That's okay.
- I'm a fan of yours.

263
00:10:32,070 --> 00:10:33,699
- That's me.
- That's her.

264
00:10:33,700 --> 00:10:34,709
(Eun Ji buys time for the kitchen by chatting with her fans.)

265
00:10:34,710 --> 00:10:35,870
- That's me.
- I told you so.

266
00:10:36,170 --> 00:10:37,770
- Please wait just a bit longer.
- Sure.

267
00:10:38,280 --> 00:10:40,040
(She's so pretty.)

268
00:10:40,240 --> 00:10:41,656
Just looking at her makes you feel full, right?

269
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:44,000
(Yu Jin appeases the customers' hunger with her cuteness.)

270
00:10:44,350 --> 00:10:46,220
We don't have enough pots for small portions.

271
00:10:46,880 --> 00:10:49,920
(While the chefs are flustered...)

272
00:10:50,490 --> 00:10:52,990
(Yu Jin runs to the kitchen with her apron fluttering.)

273
00:10:53,220 --> 00:10:54,760
You have two pots here.

274
00:10:55,160 --> 00:10:56,560
Thank you, Yu Jin.

275
00:10:56,660 --> 00:10:58,930
Please call me the fairy of pots.

276
00:10:59,330 --> 00:11:02,099
(While the service team runs around busily...)

277
00:11:02,100 --> 00:11:05,870
(to buy time for the chefs...)

278
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:09,210
- Small original tteokbokki is up.
- Okay.

279
00:11:09,740 --> 00:11:12,610
- I'll cook beef loin.
- Here's small original tteokbokki.

280
00:11:12,980 --> 00:11:14,580
Medium ghost pepper tteokbokki is ready.

281
00:11:15,780 --> 00:11:18,050
Pollack roe and clam pasta is ready.

282
00:11:19,120 --> 00:11:21,520
Here's the small original tteokbokki.

283
00:11:22,220 --> 00:11:25,119
- Your tteokbokki is here.
- It finally came out.

284
00:11:25,120 --> 00:11:27,559
I know. You waited so long, right? I'm very sorry.

285
00:11:27,560 --> 00:11:28,630
It came out fast.

286
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:32,060
(It's time to taste it quickly.)

287
00:11:33,100 --> 00:11:34,270
(Impressed)

288
00:11:34,630 --> 00:11:36,370
- Is it good?
- Yes, it's good.

289
00:11:36,770 --> 00:11:37,770
(Fortunately, they don't look like they'll send it back.)

290
00:11:37,771 --> 00:11:39,069
This could be a brilliant business item.

291
00:11:39,070 --> 00:11:40,139
(Fortunately, they don't look like they'll send it back.)

292
00:11:40,140 --> 00:11:41,169
It's good.

293
00:11:41,170 --> 00:11:43,409
(The big eaters are tasting the food as well.)

294
00:11:43,410 --> 00:11:44,980
- Here you go.
- Thank you.

295
00:11:46,080 --> 00:11:47,680
It's good. It tastes like my mom's food.

296
00:11:48,710 --> 00:11:50,709
- Hang on a second.
- I'm serious.

297
00:11:50,710 --> 00:11:52,049
- Great.
- Nice.

298
00:11:52,050 --> 00:11:53,420
- I just...
- We're doing great.

299
00:11:53,580 --> 00:11:55,319
I just heard a really touching review...

300
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:57,789
from the table that ordered everything. Can I tell you guys now?

301
00:11:57,790 --> 00:11:58,790
- Sure. Go ahead.
- Yes.

302
00:11:59,020 --> 00:12:00,489
It was so touching.

303
00:12:00,490 --> 00:12:01,559
(She's choked with emotion even before sharing the review.)

304
00:12:01,560 --> 00:12:04,160
A customer said the food tasted like his mother's food.

305
00:12:05,800 --> 00:12:06,859
(It's hard to say if that's good or bad.)

306
00:12:06,860 --> 00:12:08,670
- Really?
- He also said he'd think of you...

307
00:12:08,930 --> 00:12:11,999
- as his mother just for today.
- Really?

308
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:14,339
Oh, my. Really? It's a compliment, right?

309
00:12:14,340 --> 00:12:15,969
Young Ji, who is only 25,

310
00:12:15,970 --> 00:12:18,509
captured the true essence of a mother's cooking.

311
00:12:18,510 --> 00:12:19,750
Oh, my. That's hard to believe.

312
00:12:20,110 --> 00:12:23,009
- I applaud her achievement.
- Exactly. It's incredible.

313
00:12:23,010 --> 00:12:24,750
He said it tasted like his mother's food.

314
00:12:24,950 --> 00:12:26,150
Basil tteokbokki is remaining.

315
00:12:26,350 --> 00:12:28,289
Can you serve the basil tteokbokki as well, Yu Jin?

316
00:12:28,290 --> 00:12:30,390
- It'll be perfect timing.
- It's almost ready.

317
00:12:30,790 --> 00:12:32,859
First ready, first served.

318
00:12:32,860 --> 00:12:34,760
- Pepper.
- Cha, cha, La cucaracha

319
00:12:35,260 --> 00:12:38,099
- La cucaracha, la cucaracha - Pepper.

320
00:12:38,100 --> 00:12:39,159
(Never look up the word.)

321
00:12:39,160 --> 00:12:40,160
You're doing great.

322
00:12:40,161 --> 00:12:41,299
Can I take it now?

323
00:12:41,300 --> 00:12:43,270
- You can take it. Let's go.
- Okay.

324
00:12:43,470 --> 00:12:45,140
Store owner, here I come.

325
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:47,546
- Order complete for their table.
- That's a wrap on their table.

326
00:12:47,570 --> 00:12:49,039
(Tteokbokki Order Status: Ready and served)

327
00:12:49,040 --> 00:12:50,740
(Remaining)

328
00:12:51,210 --> 00:12:52,510
What is this again?

329
00:12:53,610 --> 00:12:55,050
- Basil.
- It's basil tteokbokki.

330
00:12:56,210 --> 00:13:00,350
(They try their first basil tteokbokki.)

331
00:13:02,120 --> 00:13:04,390
- The color is just like Shrek's.
- Right.

332
00:13:04,790 --> 00:13:06,666
It's not every day you get to taste a famous chef's cooking.

333
00:13:06,690 --> 00:13:08,630
- It's tasty.
- It's good.

334
00:13:09,190 --> 00:13:11,900
(The customers enjoy the food even though it's new to them.)

335
00:13:12,730 --> 00:13:14,169
(They already finished their food.)

336
00:13:14,170 --> 00:13:15,729
We'd like to settle up.

337
00:13:15,730 --> 00:13:17,700
Yes, sir. I'll be right with you.

338
00:13:19,140 --> 00:13:20,799
- Please come again.
- Goodbye.

339
00:13:20,800 --> 00:13:23,569
- Thank you. Have a happy day.
- Goodbye.

340
00:13:23,570 --> 00:13:26,410
Hello. Welcome. How many in your party?

341
00:13:26,540 --> 00:13:29,410
- Three.
- Three? Just a moment. I'm sorry.

342
00:13:29,880 --> 00:13:31,619
- This way, please.
- Thank you.

343
00:13:31,620 --> 00:13:32,780
(Teenage customers are here.)

344
00:13:32,820 --> 00:13:35,090
We make our own rice cakes every morning.

345
00:13:35,590 --> 00:13:38,490
We do that because our head chef said,

346
00:13:39,590 --> 00:13:42,730
"We'll just make rice cakes." That was a mistake.

347
00:13:44,230 --> 00:13:45,750
- May I sit here for a moment?
- Sure.

348
00:13:46,230 --> 00:13:48,930
(After breaking the ice, she sneaks into a seat.)

349
00:13:49,230 --> 00:13:52,700
And one medium pollack roe and clam pasta, please.

350
00:13:53,400 --> 00:13:55,840
(She comes out after taking the teens' order.)

351
00:13:56,840 --> 00:13:58,339
Table Five...

352
00:13:58,340 --> 00:13:59,900
- Has your food not come out yet?
- No.

353
00:14:00,080 --> 00:14:02,350
I see. Please give me a moment.

354
00:14:02,810 --> 00:14:06,080
I'll run to the kitchen and rush the head chef.

355
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:08,520
If we get tteokbokki too, is that going to be too much?

356
00:14:08,850 --> 00:14:10,019
- Would you like a small portion?
- Yes, please.

357
00:14:10,020 --> 00:14:11,259
- Sure. I will...
- Thank you.

358
00:14:11,260 --> 00:14:14,060
No problem. I'll add that to your order.

359
00:14:14,630 --> 00:14:17,159
Chef Lee, we got an additional order.

360
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:18,729
- Okay.
- For Table Five,

361
00:14:18,730 --> 00:14:20,299
one small original tteokbokki.

362
00:14:20,300 --> 00:14:22,600
- Got it.
- The remaining ones are...

363
00:14:22,900 --> 00:14:25,639
- one small basil tteokbokki, - A small portion.

364
00:14:25,640 --> 00:14:27,686
- one small mala tteokbokki, - One small mala tteokbokki.

365
00:14:27,710 --> 00:14:29,346
- And one small original tteokbokki.
- It'd be better...

366
00:14:29,370 --> 00:14:32,379
It'd be better if we could serve the ghost pepper tteokbokki first.

367
00:14:32,380 --> 00:14:33,879
The ghost pepper tteokbokki will be ready in one minute.

368
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:35,349
- I mean, two minutes.
- Okay.

369
00:14:35,350 --> 00:14:37,620
(Mala tteokbokki was ordered by two tables.)

370
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:41,720
(Eun Ji referred to the medium portion for the teens' table.)

371
00:14:42,290 --> 00:14:45,920
(And Young Ji is talking about the small one for the couple.)

372
00:14:46,090 --> 00:14:48,760
(One of those tables might not get their food at this rate.)

373
00:14:49,290 --> 00:14:51,660
Can I take this now? Should I clean up the table?

374
00:14:51,760 --> 00:14:52,829
- It'll be ready when you're back.
- Okay.

375
00:14:52,830 --> 00:14:55,700
- Medium ghost pepper tteokbokki.
- Thank you.

376
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:57,340
Medium ghost pepper tteokbokki?

377
00:14:57,740 --> 00:14:59,270
- I was talking to myself.
- Oh, okay.

378
00:14:59,740 --> 00:15:01,270
We haven't made any mistakes so far.

379
00:15:01,810 --> 00:15:03,309
(Hello. I am that mistake.)

380
00:15:03,310 --> 00:15:04,310
What's wrong with you?

381
00:15:04,510 --> 00:15:05,539
(Tteokbokki Order Status)

382
00:15:05,540 --> 00:15:07,680
(Medium mala tteokbokki is omitted.)

383
00:15:08,080 --> 00:15:09,879
- Eun Ji.
- Yes?

384
00:15:09,880 --> 00:15:11,549
Can I get a straw, please?

385
00:15:11,550 --> 00:15:14,219
Of course. I'll give you 2, not just 1.

386
00:15:14,220 --> 00:15:15,296
(A customer asks for help with a tiny voice.)

387
00:15:15,320 --> 00:15:16,989
- Here's a straw for you.
- Thank you.

388
00:15:16,990 --> 00:15:17,990
No problem.

389
00:15:18,090 --> 00:15:20,290
- Put it in this cup.
- It's over there.

390
00:15:20,690 --> 00:15:23,790
(The medium mala tteokbokki table is filling up on slushy.)

391
00:15:24,060 --> 00:15:25,736
Is the medium ghost pepper tteokbokki coming out?

392
00:15:25,760 --> 00:15:27,030
It's a small portion, Eun Ji.

393
00:15:29,030 --> 00:15:30,929
They ordered one more tiramisu.

394
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:31,969
- Table Two.
- And so...

395
00:15:31,970 --> 00:15:34,270
Wait, why is the ghost pepper tteokbokki small?

396
00:15:37,240 --> 00:15:38,686
Isn't the ghost pepper tteokbokki small?

397
00:15:38,710 --> 00:15:41,010
No, Table One ordered a medium.

398
00:15:42,780 --> 00:15:44,719
- Why is it a small?
- Is this ready?

399
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:46,020
Which table ordered a small?

400
00:15:46,220 --> 00:15:47,919
- Mala tteokbokki.
- I'll erase it for you.

401
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:49,520
- Thank you.
- It's mala tteokbokki.

402
00:15:49,820 --> 00:15:51,289
It's because I wrote "mala tteokbokki."

403
00:15:51,290 --> 00:15:52,570
- It's mala tteokbokki.
- I see.

404
00:15:53,190 --> 00:15:54,259
- It's correct.
- Isn't it a small size?

405
00:15:54,260 --> 00:15:55,990
- Is it a small?
- Yes, it is.

406
00:15:56,890 --> 00:15:57,899
(Eun Ji thought that it was only medium mala tteokbokki.)

407
00:15:57,900 --> 00:15:59,629
- Is it correct?
- The name is difficult.

408
00:15:59,630 --> 00:16:01,670
- We'll change the name tonight.
- Let's change it.

409
00:16:01,870 --> 00:16:05,169
Table One ordered medium ghost pepper tteokbokki.

410
00:16:05,170 --> 00:16:07,239
Can we say that there's one more medium ghost pepper tteokbokki?

411
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,439
- Yes.
- That's right.

412
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:09,639
(Thankfully, they sorted everything out without missing any orders.)

413
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:10,969
(Tteokbokki Order Status)

414
00:16:10,970 --> 00:16:12,980
(Omitted medium mala tteokbokki returns.)

415
00:16:13,240 --> 00:16:15,349
(Meanwhile, another customer walks in.)

416
00:16:15,350 --> 00:16:18,150
I'm so sorry. I'll clean it up right away.

417
00:16:19,850 --> 00:16:20,920
I'm sorry.

418
00:16:21,290 --> 00:16:24,460
It's only our second day, so we're a little overwhelmed.

419
00:16:25,690 --> 00:16:28,859
It will be one small ghost pepper tteokbokki.

420
00:16:28,860 --> 00:16:30,429
(1 small ghost pepper tteokbokki, 1 small original tteokbokki...)

421
00:16:30,430 --> 00:16:31,500
Thank you.

422
00:16:32,160 --> 00:16:34,130
(Exclaiming)

423
00:16:34,470 --> 00:16:36,170
All this trash came out of my pocket.

424
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:39,439
Small ghost pepper tteokbokki is ready.

425
00:16:39,440 --> 00:16:40,539
I'll take that.

426
00:16:40,540 --> 00:16:42,540
Wait. My goodness.

427
00:16:42,770 --> 00:16:44,979
- I'll leave it here.
- Hold on a second.

428
00:16:44,980 --> 00:16:45,980
(Eun Ji's to-do list)

429
00:16:46,110 --> 00:16:47,180
Where is it?

430
00:16:47,680 --> 00:16:48,749
(Concentrating hard while furrowing her brow)

431
00:16:48,750 --> 00:16:49,780
Table Five.

432
00:16:50,810 --> 00:16:51,849
Table Five.

433
00:16:51,850 --> 00:16:52,970
(Looking quite intimidating)

434
00:16:53,250 --> 00:16:55,420
Here's your Don't Eat Ghost Pepper Tteokbokki.

435
00:16:55,750 --> 00:16:57,989
Could you move the burner toward the center?

436
00:16:57,990 --> 00:16:59,090
- The burner...
- I see.

437
00:16:59,660 --> 00:17:01,290
I wouldn't ask for your number, would I?

438
00:17:01,890 --> 00:17:03,490
Be careful. It's hot.

439
00:17:03,730 --> 00:17:05,529
- It looks good.
- I'll bring you small plates.

440
00:17:05,530 --> 00:17:06,560
Enjoy your food.

441
00:17:07,100 --> 00:17:08,329
(Current Time: 2:55pm)

442
00:17:08,330 --> 00:17:09,929
(5 minutes before the last order)

443
00:17:09,930 --> 00:17:11,399
(Tteokbokki Order Status)

444
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:13,346
(Remaining: 2 small original, 1 medium mala, 1 small mala)

445
00:17:13,370 --> 00:17:14,740
Wait a minute. A medium mala...

446
00:17:15,240 --> 00:17:16,960
We also have one small original tteokbokki.

447
00:17:17,010 --> 00:17:18,109
Is there small original tteokbokki too?

448
00:17:18,110 --> 00:17:20,240
Yes, we got it as another order.

449
00:17:20,310 --> 00:17:22,180
We're out of pots for original tteokbokki.

450
00:17:23,280 --> 00:17:24,579
We're out of pots.

451
00:17:24,580 --> 00:17:25,580
(Everything is starting to run out.)

452
00:17:25,581 --> 00:17:26,620
The original...

453
00:17:28,120 --> 00:17:31,160
(Yu Jin is serving dongchimi.)

454
00:17:32,990 --> 00:17:34,470
Gosh, I'm out of bowls for dongchimi.

455
00:17:35,430 --> 00:17:39,400
(Hunting for hidden bowls for dongchimi)

456
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:41,580
Look how fast the fried food is going out.

457
00:17:44,670 --> 00:17:46,799
Oh, no. We're out of fried toppings.

458
00:17:46,800 --> 00:17:48,600
(The prepared fried food starts running out.)

459
00:17:52,610 --> 00:17:54,039
(She burns what's left.)

460
00:17:54,040 --> 00:17:56,350
I thought I had already taken it out.

461
00:17:57,750 --> 00:18:00,820
(Crying her eyes out)

462
00:18:03,120 --> 00:18:04,249
This is...

463
00:18:04,250 --> 00:18:05,389
(As the ingredients...)

464
00:18:05,390 --> 00:18:06,489
It's insane.

465
00:18:06,490 --> 00:18:08,136
(And everyone's mental energy is running out.)

466
00:18:08,160 --> 00:18:09,259
We can do it.

467
00:18:09,260 --> 00:18:11,600
(Everyone is finally making a run for the finish line.)

468
00:18:11,830 --> 00:18:14,770
Oh, no. This is so unfortunate.

469
00:18:15,300 --> 00:18:16,969
Didn't you hear the news?

470
00:18:16,970 --> 00:18:17,970
(A customer already walked in.)

471
00:18:17,971 --> 00:18:18,999
Oh, my gosh.

472
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,599
We are two minutes away from last order.

473
00:18:20,600 --> 00:18:22,740
Two minutes away? Please come on in.

474
00:18:23,770 --> 00:18:27,340
(They give a warm welcome, but their bodies say otherwise.)

475
00:18:27,980 --> 00:18:29,749
- How many are you?
- I'm alone.

476
00:18:29,750 --> 00:18:31,079
Welcome. Come this way.

477
00:18:31,080 --> 00:18:32,080
(You're always welcome at Space Rice Cake.)

478
00:18:32,081 --> 00:18:33,980
One small original tteokbokki.

479
00:18:34,150 --> 00:18:35,519
One coffee slushy.

480
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:36,590
I'm about to cry.

481
00:18:37,090 --> 00:18:38,660
Mimi, is this it?

482
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:40,859
- Wait.
- Right now...

483
00:18:40,860 --> 00:18:42,029
I just have to heat it up.

484
00:18:42,030 --> 00:18:43,290
I'm sorry, but I burned it.

485
00:18:46,400 --> 00:18:47,560
Viewers.

486
00:18:48,070 --> 00:18:49,400
Are you still there?

487
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,300
If you're there, come and chop some fishcakes.

488
00:18:52,400 --> 00:18:53,940
(No response to the fishcakes)

489
00:18:54,240 --> 00:18:56,640
(Mimi chops the fishcakes.)

490
00:18:56,770 --> 00:18:58,139
It'll be ready in 1 minute 30 seconds.

491
00:18:58,140 --> 00:19:00,710
(The head chef is making 3 pans of tteokbokki.)

492
00:19:01,110 --> 00:19:04,410
I love you, customers.

493
00:19:04,620 --> 00:19:06,449
- Will they be ready together?
- Yes.

494
00:19:06,450 --> 00:19:08,020
That's great. This is it.

495
00:19:08,850 --> 00:19:11,620
It's the last order, so I'm throwing in all the fried food.

496
00:19:11,790 --> 00:19:13,659
Give them to me. I'll serve them all like this.

497
00:19:13,660 --> 00:19:14,989
They aren't ready yet.

498
00:19:14,990 --> 00:19:15,990
(Putting everything she's got)

499
00:19:15,991 --> 00:19:17,529
- I'll serve the original.
- We can go together.

500
00:19:17,530 --> 00:19:18,699
I need this.

501
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:21,230
- The food is ready.
- Can you top it with meat?

502
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:24,800
Excuse me. Don't Eat Ghost Pepper Tteokbokki.

503
00:19:25,570 --> 00:19:27,369
Here's your small original tteokbokki.

504
00:19:27,370 --> 00:19:29,269
- Here you go.
- I'll take your glove.

505
00:19:29,270 --> 00:19:30,430
(Serving the last tteokbokki)

506
00:19:35,050 --> 00:19:36,480
(Humming)

507
00:19:36,610 --> 00:19:37,810
- Is it good?
- Yes.

508
00:19:39,380 --> 00:19:40,419
(Even the customer who came alone)

509
00:19:40,420 --> 00:19:42,249
- This is good.
- Yes.

510
00:19:42,250 --> 00:19:45,990
(Nodding with satisfaction)

511
00:19:47,260 --> 00:19:48,629
Yes, sir.

512
00:19:48,630 --> 00:19:51,229
I really love and respect you all.

513
00:19:51,230 --> 00:19:54,299
Credit card, 40.5 dollars.

514
00:19:54,300 --> 00:19:55,969
- Is the total correct?
- Yes.

515
00:19:55,970 --> 00:19:58,170
It's easier to ask you.

516
00:19:58,900 --> 00:20:01,100
The total is 28 dollars.

517
00:20:01,810 --> 00:20:03,510
Fifty-dollar bill?

518
00:20:03,910 --> 00:20:05,870
If you give me 50 dollars, how much do I owe you?

519
00:20:06,380 --> 00:20:08,309
Twenty-two dollars. Thank you.

520
00:20:08,310 --> 00:20:10,379
- Thank you for the food.
- Thank you.

521
00:20:10,380 --> 00:20:12,549
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

522
00:20:12,550 --> 00:20:13,919
(When the last customers leave, )

523
00:20:13,920 --> 00:20:16,620
(it's finally a moment for them to catch their breath.)

524
00:20:16,720 --> 00:20:19,390
The first day of Space Rice Cake's business is closed.

525
00:20:21,360 --> 00:20:23,389
(It's their 2nd day.)

526
00:20:23,390 --> 00:20:24,529
Thank you.

527
00:20:24,530 --> 00:20:26,200
(Closed for business)

528
00:20:26,500 --> 00:20:28,930
- Mimi, I'll do it.
- I just started.

529
00:20:29,230 --> 00:20:30,630
Young Ji, you need to take a break.

530
00:20:30,930 --> 00:20:32,800
Yu Jin, didn't we do really well today?

531
00:20:33,870 --> 00:20:35,039
Were we fully booked the whole time?

532
00:20:35,040 --> 00:20:36,769
I was too busy making tteokbokki...

533
00:20:36,770 --> 00:20:37,940
to know what was going on.

534
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:39,239
Didn't we do very well?

535
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:41,116
(The head chef wants to know how big today's business was.)

536
00:20:41,140 --> 00:20:43,020
It felt like it was twice as much as yesterday.

537
00:20:43,080 --> 00:20:44,979
But in actual numbers, it must be 1.8 times as much.

538
00:20:44,980 --> 00:20:48,689
How was the overall response to Broccolino Basiliano?

539
00:20:48,690 --> 00:20:50,349
- People loved it.
- Did they?

540
00:20:50,350 --> 00:20:52,489
Those who love creamy dishes went crazy for it.

541
00:20:52,490 --> 00:20:53,490
Right?

542
00:20:54,020 --> 00:20:55,289
How did you sell it so well?

543
00:20:55,290 --> 00:20:57,059
The name is so difficult,

544
00:20:57,060 --> 00:20:58,600
yet so many people ordered it.

545
00:20:59,200 --> 00:21:01,299
What did you say to make them order it?

546
00:21:01,300 --> 00:21:02,370
(Making a compliment)

547
00:21:02,430 --> 00:21:03,670
It was all because of the food.

548
00:21:04,230 --> 00:21:05,239
As expected,

549
00:21:05,240 --> 00:21:07,146
you're Korea's number 1 salesperson and number 1 comedienne.

550
00:21:07,170 --> 00:21:09,809
- And Baeksang Arts Awards winner.
- Nice.

551
00:21:09,810 --> 00:21:10,969
She's soon to be an Oscar winner.

552
00:21:10,970 --> 00:21:12,279
I already won the Baeksang Arts Award.

553
00:21:12,280 --> 00:21:14,009
The Grammys, the Oscars,

554
00:21:14,010 --> 00:21:15,109
and the Blue Dragon Film Awards are left.

555
00:21:15,110 --> 00:21:16,149
Thank you.

556
00:21:16,150 --> 00:21:18,119
- You'll win those awards soon.
- Thank you.

557
00:21:18,120 --> 00:21:19,720
Start practicing your acceptance speech.

558
00:21:20,850 --> 00:21:22,649
I don't know why my back hurts so much.

559
00:21:22,650 --> 00:21:25,289
Have a seat. Let's stop for a second.

560
00:21:25,290 --> 00:21:26,389
It's so exhausting...

561
00:21:26,390 --> 00:21:27,419
Mimi, could you stop for a second?

562
00:21:27,420 --> 00:21:29,129
It's so exhausting, but it's so much fun.

563
00:21:29,130 --> 00:21:31,630
- Yes, it's fun.
- It's fun but it's exhausting.

564
00:21:31,960 --> 00:21:34,829
(She's happy but exhausted.)

565
00:21:34,830 --> 00:21:37,330
We need to take a break to keep running our business later.

566
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:39,339
- There's a lot of stuff.
- What?

567
00:21:39,340 --> 00:21:41,340
Isn't it the crab cream croquette?

568
00:21:41,440 --> 00:21:42,440
That's amazing.

569
00:21:42,441 --> 00:21:44,209
- A croquette?
- It's available only in the summer.

570
00:21:44,210 --> 00:21:45,579
- You can eat it only in the summer.
- Oh, my.

571
00:21:45,580 --> 00:21:46,839
- We must eat it now.
- Yes, we do.

572
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:47,939
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

573
00:21:47,940 --> 00:21:50,410
(Clinking in a good mood)

574
00:21:52,280 --> 00:21:53,350
It's so good.

575
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:54,990
There's crab meat inside.

576
00:21:55,020 --> 00:21:56,990
- This feels like summer.
- Yes.

577
00:21:57,490 --> 00:21:59,489
Eun Ji, these are churros.

578
00:21:59,490 --> 00:22:00,689
Take a look at the churros.

579
00:22:00,690 --> 00:22:01,850
(Mimi spots something sweet.)

580
00:22:01,890 --> 00:22:02,959
I'll sprinkle it on.

581
00:22:02,960 --> 00:22:04,430
(Lightly sprinkling powdered sugar)

582
00:22:04,590 --> 00:22:05,599
(Shaking)

583
00:22:05,600 --> 00:22:07,240
This is exactly what Mimi goes crazy for.

584
00:22:07,630 --> 00:22:09,230
The caramel smell is insane.

585
00:22:09,830 --> 00:22:10,830
(Humming)

586
00:22:10,831 --> 00:22:11,840
It makes me feel so good.

587
00:22:12,600 --> 00:22:13,699
There's cream.

588
00:22:13,700 --> 00:22:15,839
(Caramel cream)

589
00:22:15,840 --> 00:22:17,509
After taking a bite of this, Mimi came back.

590
00:22:17,510 --> 00:22:18,910
It shooed away the jeolpyeon ghost.

591
00:22:19,210 --> 00:22:20,780
Have some chicken with the sauce.

592
00:22:22,150 --> 00:22:23,180
You're eating it without?

593
00:22:23,750 --> 00:22:24,779
This is good.

594
00:22:24,780 --> 00:22:26,649
(It hits her taste buds.)

595
00:22:26,650 --> 00:22:28,620
- I feel so happy.
- Chicken drumstick.

596
00:22:29,790 --> 00:22:30,819
It's so delicious.

597
00:22:30,820 --> 00:22:34,290
(Summer snacks you must enjoy before summer ends)

598
00:22:34,660 --> 00:22:36,359
(After the happy snack break)

599
00:22:36,360 --> 00:22:38,600
Yes, this is good. Let's go.

600
00:22:39,630 --> 00:22:40,860
It's not over yet.

601
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:43,000
I'm going to make cream bread.

602
00:22:43,001 --> 00:22:44,470
Gosh, they look so cute.

603
00:22:45,300 --> 00:22:46,970
They look exactly like Torong.

604
00:22:47,340 --> 00:22:48,569
Mini gijeongtteok.

605
00:22:48,570 --> 00:22:50,346
(Made by fermenting non-glutinous rice flour with makgeolli)

606
00:22:50,370 --> 00:22:51,410
Didn't I leave...

607
00:22:52,440 --> 00:22:54,880
a message to Producer Ye Seul?

608
00:22:55,180 --> 00:22:57,450
(Some days before the opening of Space Rice Cake)

609
00:22:57,780 --> 00:23:00,950
(Mimi proposed a dessert idea.)

610
00:23:01,550 --> 00:23:03,249
(What if we cut grilled rice cake in half and fill it with cream?)

611
00:23:03,250 --> 00:23:04,250
(That's a great idea. We'll fully support you.)

612
00:23:04,251 --> 00:23:05,859
(The headquarters liked the idea...)

613
00:23:05,860 --> 00:23:07,420
(and decided to provide gijeongtteok.)

614
00:23:07,520 --> 00:23:09,089
In Bangkok,

615
00:23:09,090 --> 00:23:10,229
there was something really interesting.

616
00:23:10,230 --> 00:23:11,729
I was walking around, and I saw someone grill...

617
00:23:11,730 --> 00:23:13,629
- bread on a gridiron.
- Bread?

618
00:23:13,630 --> 00:23:15,869
Yes, bread.

619
00:23:15,870 --> 00:23:18,099
They cut it in half, filled it with cream,

620
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:19,970
and served it like this as street food.

621
00:23:20,470 --> 00:23:22,709
(Yaowarat toasted buns, Thai street dessert...)

622
00:23:22,710 --> 00:23:24,909
(made with grilled bread filled with cream)

623
00:23:24,910 --> 00:23:26,609
It was so good.

624
00:23:26,610 --> 00:23:28,626
If we make it with rice cake, it'd work 100 percent.

625
00:23:28,650 --> 00:23:31,280
(Cooking starts.)

626
00:23:31,580 --> 00:23:33,780
This is very simple.

627
00:23:35,190 --> 00:23:37,820
(Mimi reveals her signature rice cake dessert recipe.)

628
00:23:38,320 --> 00:23:42,390
(First, brush melted butter onto a sheet of parchment paper.)

629
00:23:42,490 --> 00:23:45,459
(Line up the gijeongtteok.)

630
00:23:45,460 --> 00:23:47,599
(Brush each piece evenly with butter.)

631
00:23:47,600 --> 00:23:49,199
These are all done.

632
00:23:49,200 --> 00:23:51,669
(This helps make the outside crispy, the inside moist.)

633
00:23:51,670 --> 00:23:52,740
Okay.

634
00:23:52,970 --> 00:23:54,199
For ten minutes.

635
00:23:54,200 --> 00:23:56,310
(Into the oven for an upgrade in texture and color)

636
00:23:56,440 --> 00:24:00,179
(After a 10-minute tanning session)

637
00:24:00,180 --> 00:24:01,580
They look done.

638
00:24:01,850 --> 00:24:04,009
Mimi, the color looks so beautiful.

639
00:24:04,010 --> 00:24:05,380
I want to try one.

640
00:24:05,850 --> 00:24:07,920
- Aren't they pretty?
- They look delicious.

641
00:24:08,220 --> 00:24:10,450
Ta-da.

642
00:24:10,820 --> 00:24:12,060
Mimi, what is it called?

643
00:24:12,420 --> 00:24:13,459
Cream rice cake.

644
00:24:13,460 --> 00:24:14,460
(The baked gijeongtteok comes out fluffy.)

645
00:24:14,461 --> 00:24:18,160
(Next is making the cream.)

646
00:24:18,300 --> 00:24:19,660
I'll start with matcha.

647
00:24:21,230 --> 00:24:24,070
Three tablespoons of matcha.

648
00:24:24,840 --> 00:24:26,470
- Do I just stir it?
- Yes.

649
00:24:26,770 --> 00:24:30,970
(A mascarpone-based cream...)

650
00:24:31,040 --> 00:24:34,339
(paired with the bittersweet flavor of matcha)

651
00:24:34,340 --> 00:24:35,949
(Next is the chocolate cream.)

652
00:24:35,950 --> 00:24:37,049
One.

653
00:24:37,050 --> 00:24:40,580
Mimi, it's going to be one incredible dessert.

654
00:24:40,980 --> 00:24:42,089
Thank you.

655
00:24:42,090 --> 00:24:43,090
(A sweet, delicious flavor that puts you in a good mood)

656
00:24:43,091 --> 00:24:44,120
This is really...

657
00:24:45,860 --> 00:24:47,459
Here you go. Try it.

658
00:24:47,460 --> 00:24:48,859
How did you make this?

659
00:24:48,860 --> 00:24:51,629
It's chocolate cream. I'm wondering if it should be richer than this.

660
00:24:51,630 --> 00:24:53,529
I usually like it richer.

661
00:24:53,530 --> 00:24:54,530
(Carefully)

662
00:24:55,230 --> 00:24:57,429
- Gosh, it's good.
- Is it good enough?

663
00:24:57,430 --> 00:24:58,899
- I want it to be richer.
- Really?

664
00:24:58,900 --> 00:25:01,610
Add one more spoon. My taste is on the mild side.

665
00:25:02,610 --> 00:25:05,210
- Gosh, it makes me feel good.
- It's delicious.

666
00:25:05,380 --> 00:25:08,140
- It's delicious.
- You're good at making desserts.

667
00:25:08,380 --> 00:25:10,910
This is definitely going to be delicious.

668
00:25:11,780 --> 00:25:12,780
Here you go, Yu Jin.

669
00:25:12,781 --> 00:25:15,019
(Tasting the chocolate cream again)

670
00:25:15,020 --> 00:25:17,149
Yu Jin, tell her what you think.

671
00:25:17,150 --> 00:25:19,550
(This time, it's the richer version of the chocolate cream.)

672
00:25:19,760 --> 00:25:21,519
- It's good.
- Is it nice?

673
00:25:21,520 --> 00:25:23,029
- It's good.
- Okay.

674
00:25:23,030 --> 00:25:24,059
(Grinning from ear to ear)

675
00:25:24,060 --> 00:25:25,100
It's good.

676
00:25:25,260 --> 00:25:26,960
Split it in half like this.

677
00:25:27,760 --> 00:25:29,669
(Once you cut open the browned rice cake to reveal the inside)

678
00:25:29,670 --> 00:25:32,669
I'll squeeze this in between here.

679
00:25:32,670 --> 00:25:33,699
Okay.

680
00:25:33,700 --> 00:25:35,016
(Filling it generously with cream)

681
00:25:35,040 --> 00:25:37,039
It'd be nice if we had a tray.

682
00:25:37,040 --> 00:25:38,680
A tray?

683
00:25:38,740 --> 00:25:40,580
To use it for what?

684
00:25:41,010 --> 00:25:42,949
- Can you give me a sheet...
- Is this right?

685
00:25:42,950 --> 00:25:43,950
Of parchment paper?

686
00:25:43,951 --> 00:25:46,220
Mimi, you're a dessert master.

687
00:25:46,680 --> 00:25:47,780
Thank you.

688
00:25:48,250 --> 00:25:51,420
(Shall we try the matcha and chocolate cream rice cake?)

689
00:25:52,090 --> 00:25:53,389
Try some of this, Young Ji.

690
00:25:53,390 --> 00:25:54,659
(Eating)

691
00:25:54,660 --> 00:25:55,660
Thank you.

692
00:25:56,330 --> 00:25:57,390
See how it tastes.

693
00:25:59,300 --> 00:26:02,230
Mimi, this is unbelievable.

694
00:26:02,600 --> 00:26:04,100
- It tastes so good.
- Mimi.

695
00:26:05,040 --> 00:26:06,739
How much should we sell this for? It's so good.

696
00:26:06,740 --> 00:26:08,170
Wait, we have to sell this.

697
00:26:09,070 --> 00:26:10,309
It's really good.

698
00:26:10,310 --> 00:26:12,010
- Can you believe this?
- It's so good.

699
00:26:12,780 --> 00:26:14,860
What should we do? Should we start selling it today?

700
00:26:15,010 --> 00:26:16,479
- Maybe we can give it out...
- As an appetizer?

701
00:26:16,480 --> 00:26:18,480
As an appetizer today.

702
00:26:18,850 --> 00:26:21,210
If we're going to sell it officially, let's start tomorrow.

703
00:26:21,580 --> 00:26:23,249
We'll give two per table.

704
00:26:23,250 --> 00:26:24,289
Okay.

705
00:26:24,290 --> 00:26:26,560
(30 minutes before opening)

706
00:26:26,790 --> 00:26:28,089
(A final prep sprint)

707
00:26:28,090 --> 00:26:29,260
Scissors.

708
00:26:30,660 --> 00:26:34,970
(While the kitchen team is prepping the main dishes, )

709
00:26:35,070 --> 00:26:38,270
(the dessert team starts prepping the new menu item.)

710
00:26:38,500 --> 00:26:39,839
Split it in half.

711
00:26:39,840 --> 00:26:41,546
(Taking it step by step like they were taught)

712
00:26:41,570 --> 00:26:43,069
(Sawing through the gijeongtteok)

713
00:26:43,070 --> 00:26:44,639
- Split it in half.
- Yes.

714
00:26:44,640 --> 00:26:46,140
Cut it deep enough.

715
00:26:46,680 --> 00:26:48,110
In the middle... My goodness.

716
00:26:49,350 --> 00:26:51,510
(The opening is way too wide.)

717
00:26:51,650 --> 00:26:52,819
(Feeling intimidated)

718
00:26:52,820 --> 00:26:54,019
- Is it a failure?
- No.

719
00:26:54,020 --> 00:26:55,719
- In the middle...
- This is okay for today.

720
00:26:55,720 --> 00:26:57,720
It's okay if the cream sticks out.

721
00:26:58,790 --> 00:27:00,090
There isn't enough cream.

722
00:27:00,320 --> 00:27:02,430
(She tries her best.)

723
00:27:02,790 --> 00:27:05,430
This one isn't quite right, is it?

724
00:27:05,560 --> 00:27:07,560
(They just laugh nervously.)

725
00:27:07,700 --> 00:27:08,799
It's an appetizer, so it's okay.

726
00:27:08,800 --> 00:27:10,129
It's okay even if they don't look...

727
00:27:10,130 --> 00:27:11,470
- pretty today.
- Okay.

728
00:27:11,570 --> 00:27:12,740
I'll go and turn the sign.

729
00:27:16,970 --> 00:27:19,079
(It's time to turn the sign around for business.)

730
00:27:19,080 --> 00:27:22,510
Sticky rice cakes

731
00:27:23,150 --> 00:27:26,250
Garaetteok

732
00:27:26,750 --> 00:27:29,789
(Open for business)

733
00:27:29,790 --> 00:27:32,590
Baekseoltteok

734
00:27:33,120 --> 00:27:34,990
We're selling rice cakes.

735
00:27:35,590 --> 00:27:39,030
Nice. We're starting.

736
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:40,400
Chef Kim Mi Hyun, honesty.

737
00:27:40,860 --> 00:27:42,129
- Humility. Ahk.
- Ahk.

738
00:27:42,130 --> 00:27:43,329
- I love you.
- I love you.

739
00:27:43,330 --> 00:27:44,330
I love you.

740
00:27:44,331 --> 00:27:46,170
(Meanwhile, the server is relaxed.)

741
00:27:46,500 --> 00:27:49,440
(Strutting casually out the front door)

742
00:27:49,570 --> 00:27:50,610
Everyone.

743
00:27:51,410 --> 00:27:52,680
What brings you here?

744
00:27:53,380 --> 00:27:55,879
(Appearing before the innocent little lambs)

745
00:27:55,880 --> 00:27:58,080
(A scary older sister)

746
00:27:58,350 --> 00:27:59,850
- Are there three of you?
- Yes.

747
00:28:00,520 --> 00:28:01,619
Did you get permission...

748
00:28:01,620 --> 00:28:02,690
- from your mom?
- Yes.

749
00:28:02,850 --> 00:28:04,019
Why don't you introduce yourselves?

750
00:28:04,020 --> 00:28:05,500
(They finish introducing themselves.)

751
00:28:05,660 --> 00:28:07,220
Seo Hyun, Ji Woo, So Hyun.

752
00:28:07,920 --> 00:28:08,990
Please come in.

753
00:28:09,590 --> 00:28:11,360
Come all the way inside.

754
00:28:12,730 --> 00:28:16,130
This is Space Rice Cake restaurant,

755
00:28:16,430 --> 00:28:18,100
so you'll need to pay before you leave.

756
00:28:18,370 --> 00:28:19,539
- Are you ready?
- Yes.

757
00:28:19,540 --> 00:28:20,869
Take a seat at Table One.

758
00:28:20,870 --> 00:28:23,070
- Take a look at the menu.
- Okay.

759
00:28:23,540 --> 00:28:25,839
We have customers at Table One.

760
00:28:25,840 --> 00:28:29,210
They're the cutest little girls in third grade.

761
00:28:29,580 --> 00:28:31,310
- Three third-graders?
- Yes.

762
00:28:32,050 --> 00:28:35,819
I told them, "We actually charge money here."

763
00:28:35,820 --> 00:28:37,419
"Did you tell your moms that you were coming?"

764
00:28:37,420 --> 00:28:38,560
They said, "Yes."

765
00:28:38,720 --> 00:28:39,819
"Is that so?"

766
00:28:39,820 --> 00:28:41,120
How did you talk to them?

767
00:28:41,790 --> 00:28:42,790
"This is..."

768
00:28:42,791 --> 00:28:43,960
(Intimidating)

769
00:28:44,130 --> 00:28:45,130
This is insane.

770
00:28:45,131 --> 00:28:46,611
(The little customers finally relax.)

771
00:28:46,660 --> 00:28:48,000
There are photos up there.

772
00:28:48,400 --> 00:28:49,469
- That's crazy.
- My gosh.

773
00:28:49,470 --> 00:28:50,529
(Somewhat artificial-looking photos of them making rice cakes)

774
00:28:50,530 --> 00:28:52,440
They have everything here.

775
00:28:52,640 --> 00:28:54,739
It looks like they make rice cakes from scratch.

776
00:28:54,740 --> 00:28:56,486
- That's so funny.
- Seo Hyun, Ji Woo, and So Hyun.

777
00:28:56,510 --> 00:28:58,610
- They said our names.
- They said our names.

778
00:28:58,780 --> 00:29:00,410
(They suddenly get nervous again.)

779
00:29:00,910 --> 00:29:02,910
- Did you look at the menu?
- Yes.

780
00:29:02,950 --> 00:29:04,379
- May I take your order?
- Yes.

781
00:29:04,380 --> 00:29:05,419
Okay.

782
00:29:05,420 --> 00:29:07,449
Three original tteokbokki...

783
00:29:07,450 --> 00:29:09,390
and one soda, please.

784
00:29:09,720 --> 00:29:10,720
Okay.

785
00:29:10,721 --> 00:29:12,890
Did you mean three small original tteokbokki?

786
00:29:13,460 --> 00:29:14,920
A small for each of you?

787
00:29:15,330 --> 00:29:17,329
Okay, I'll put in your order.

788
00:29:17,330 --> 00:29:18,330
- Okay.
- Okay.

789
00:29:19,100 --> 00:29:20,729
Am I scary when I talk?

790
00:29:20,730 --> 00:29:22,000
- No.
- No, right?

791
00:29:22,130 --> 00:29:23,670
- Right.
- Thank you.

792
00:29:24,230 --> 00:29:25,699
- Will you buy...
- Get your money out.

793
00:29:25,700 --> 00:29:27,840
- If you have one more bill...
- Okay.

794
00:29:28,070 --> 00:29:29,610
This should be enough.

795
00:29:29,970 --> 00:29:32,479
(They set it aside carefully.)

796
00:29:32,480 --> 00:29:33,480
What do you think?

797
00:29:33,580 --> 00:29:35,680
Give them a variety. This one is chocolate.

798
00:29:35,980 --> 00:29:36,980
It's ready.

799
00:29:37,980 --> 00:29:40,120
This is cream gijeongtteok.

800
00:29:40,380 --> 00:29:43,420
We're trying to decide whether to make it a new menu item.

801
00:29:43,590 --> 00:29:45,319
I'd love for you to try it...

802
00:29:45,320 --> 00:29:46,860
and tell me what you think.

803
00:29:47,490 --> 00:29:48,889
Your food will be ready soon.

804
00:29:48,890 --> 00:29:50,289
(After explaining it at their eye level)

805
00:29:50,290 --> 00:29:51,359
(Sneaking a little glance)

806
00:29:51,360 --> 00:29:52,800
Her face is so small and pretty.

807
00:29:54,760 --> 00:29:57,670
(They calm down and taste the cream rice cakes.)

808
00:29:58,270 --> 00:29:59,840
- It's crispy.
- It's delicious.

809
00:29:59,900 --> 00:30:01,240
Yes, it's crunchy.

810
00:30:01,300 --> 00:30:02,970
- It could be a new menu item.
- I agree.

811
00:30:03,440 --> 00:30:04,840
It tastes like butter tteok.

812
00:30:05,210 --> 00:30:06,210
I can smell the butter.

813
00:30:07,080 --> 00:30:09,110
I wonder why they don't sell it.

814
00:30:09,910 --> 00:30:11,950
- This is really delicious.
- I know.

815
00:30:12,950 --> 00:30:14,019
(Shy girls' table: 3 small original tteokbokki)

816
00:30:14,020 --> 00:30:15,049
(1 soda)

817
00:30:15,050 --> 00:30:17,049
- Eun Ji.
- Yes?

818
00:30:17,050 --> 00:30:18,449
Is this order correct?

819
00:30:18,450 --> 00:30:19,819
Did they really make this order?

820
00:30:19,820 --> 00:30:21,889
Each of them wants one small tteokbokki.

821
00:30:21,890 --> 00:30:23,360
They're definitely MZers.

822
00:30:23,390 --> 00:30:25,999
I think the three of them are pitching in.

823
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:27,059
- They're paying separately.
- Separately?

824
00:30:27,060 --> 00:30:28,830
Is that right? I understand now.

825
00:30:29,100 --> 00:30:30,929
(Getting ready to spring into action)

826
00:30:30,930 --> 00:30:32,040
I'll do it all at once.

827
00:30:32,770 --> 00:30:34,999
It's my first time getting three orders...

828
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:36,740
of the original tteokbokki.

829
00:30:37,170 --> 00:30:38,739
I'll put all three in at exactly the same time.

830
00:30:38,740 --> 00:30:40,710
They look cute. Did we make them today?

831
00:30:41,010 --> 00:30:43,050
- Yes, they're freshly made.
- They look delicious.

832
00:30:43,510 --> 00:30:44,579
It's ready.

833
00:30:44,580 --> 00:30:46,580
(Adding 3 garaetteok at the same time)

834
00:30:46,880 --> 00:30:48,850
(Serious)

835
00:30:49,220 --> 00:30:51,120
(Mimi's frying factory is up and running.)

836
00:30:51,350 --> 00:30:53,590
(A generous portion)

837
00:30:53,760 --> 00:30:55,190
Gosh, it looks incredible.

838
00:30:55,690 --> 00:30:56,829
They're going out at the same time.

839
00:30:56,830 --> 00:30:58,860
We'll make sure that they stay friends.

840
00:30:59,530 --> 00:31:01,360
- Let's go. Gosh.
- That's right.

841
00:31:01,730 --> 00:31:04,030
This is great. Fast service is the best.

842
00:31:04,300 --> 00:31:07,199
Your three orders of original tteokbokki are here.

843
00:31:07,200 --> 00:31:08,869
The pot is extremely hot.

844
00:31:08,870 --> 00:31:10,939
- The pot is very hot.
- Don't touch it.

845
00:31:10,940 --> 00:31:12,240
Don't touch it.

846
00:31:12,610 --> 00:31:13,840
Don't touch it.

847
00:31:14,280 --> 00:31:16,410
We're off to a great start.

848
00:31:16,750 --> 00:31:18,620
Why is it so calm? I like it.

849
00:31:18,650 --> 00:31:20,556
Three orders of tteokbokki in seven minutes. How's that?

850
00:31:20,580 --> 00:31:21,879
Three orders of tteokbokki in seven minutes?

851
00:31:21,880 --> 00:31:22,889
That's insane.

852
00:31:22,890 --> 00:31:24,019
Do you need help with anything?

853
00:31:24,020 --> 00:31:25,760
Things are very calm for us now.

854
00:31:26,320 --> 00:31:27,690
When ten people walk in,

855
00:31:28,290 --> 00:31:29,530
things will be very different.

856
00:31:29,790 --> 00:31:31,660
(Here's what she means by ten people.)

857
00:31:32,230 --> 00:31:34,400
(After closing yesterday)

858
00:31:34,560 --> 00:31:38,470
We already took our last order.

859
00:31:38,870 --> 00:31:41,239
- I'll make a reservation for you.
- Thank you.

860
00:31:41,240 --> 00:31:43,410
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

861
00:31:43,870 --> 00:31:47,010
(Setting up the reserved tables in advance)

862
00:31:47,610 --> 00:31:50,580
Then we'll do it like this.

863
00:31:50,780 --> 00:31:52,250
We're expecting ten people.

864
00:31:52,950 --> 00:31:54,479
- Right.
- I think they're coming now.

865
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:55,519
Here comes the mini-van.

866
00:31:55,520 --> 00:31:56,649
Are they here yet?

867
00:31:56,650 --> 00:31:58,220
(Space Rice Cake)

868
00:31:58,620 --> 00:32:01,190
(An enormous parade of customers)

869
00:32:01,520 --> 00:32:04,060
(Walking in with confidence)

870
00:32:04,530 --> 00:32:05,600
They're coming.

871
00:32:06,100 --> 00:32:07,200
They're coming, right?

872
00:32:07,660 --> 00:32:08,829
They're coming.

873
00:32:08,830 --> 00:32:10,029
Gosh, they're here.

874
00:32:10,030 --> 00:32:12,239
- Hello.
- Hello.

875
00:32:12,240 --> 00:32:13,240
There are ten of us.

876
00:32:13,241 --> 00:32:14,969
- Please come this way.
- The ten who made a reservation.

877
00:32:14,970 --> 00:32:17,070
We marked the reserved tables for you.

878
00:32:17,410 --> 00:32:18,440
Thank you.

879
00:32:18,640 --> 00:32:20,280
Head chef, are you ready?

880
00:32:20,510 --> 00:32:22,050
Honestly, I'm not ready.

881
00:32:22,250 --> 00:32:24,170
But it has nothing to do with how prepared I am.

882
00:32:24,250 --> 00:32:25,849
(It looks like the Last Supper.)

883
00:32:25,850 --> 00:32:26,919
You don't want it?

884
00:32:26,920 --> 00:32:28,119
- We should try everything.
- Right.

885
00:32:28,120 --> 00:32:29,120
We need to try everything.

886
00:32:29,121 --> 00:32:30,319
Besides, we eat a lot.

887
00:32:30,320 --> 00:32:31,349
We must order a lot.

888
00:32:31,350 --> 00:32:32,836
- We should order the desserts now.
- Right.

889
00:32:32,860 --> 00:32:35,340
- We must order everything at once.
- Mom, can I get a slushy?

890
00:32:35,590 --> 00:32:38,159
I'm expecting the group of five to order...

891
00:32:38,160 --> 00:32:39,560
- an insane amount of food.
- Okay.

892
00:32:39,800 --> 00:32:41,760
- We'd like to order.
- Okay.

893
00:32:42,330 --> 00:32:44,700
(Finally, it's the moment of truth.)

894
00:32:44,900 --> 00:32:46,180
I expect three orders of medium.

895
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:48,669
Or it could be four orders.

896
00:32:48,670 --> 00:32:49,769
(Feeling empty)

897
00:32:49,770 --> 00:32:50,770
Four orders of medium?

898
00:32:50,910 --> 00:32:52,309
- Are you sure? Not a medium?
- Okay.

899
00:32:52,310 --> 00:32:54,109
- Do we have to order one...
- Yes?

900
00:32:54,110 --> 00:32:55,349
Jade Emperor Tteokbokki per person?

901
00:32:55,350 --> 00:32:57,430
- Isn't it per person?
- Is it one order per person?

902
00:32:57,580 --> 00:32:59,379
The Jade Emperor challenge is available...

903
00:32:59,380 --> 00:33:01,749
for up to four people.

904
00:33:01,750 --> 00:33:03,289
- Then let's order just 1.
- Just 1.

905
00:33:03,290 --> 00:33:04,290
Just one? Okay.

906
00:33:04,291 --> 00:33:05,760
I'll put in this order.

907
00:33:06,120 --> 00:33:10,090
(The biggest group ever makes the head chef nervous.)

908
00:33:12,760 --> 00:33:14,999
May I start reading the order?

909
00:33:15,000 --> 00:33:16,000
I'm ready.

910
00:33:16,800 --> 00:33:18,939
Two medium...

911
00:33:18,940 --> 00:33:20,199
- original tteokbokki.
- Okay.

912
00:33:20,200 --> 00:33:22,239
One medium...

913
00:33:22,240 --> 00:33:23,309
- ghost pepper tteokbokki.
- Okay.

914
00:33:23,310 --> 00:33:24,869
One order...

915
00:33:24,870 --> 00:33:26,109
- of Jade Emperor Tteokbokki.
- Okay.

916
00:33:26,110 --> 00:33:27,879
Two orders of pollack roe and clam pasta.

917
00:33:27,880 --> 00:33:29,049
(Large group table's order)

918
00:33:29,050 --> 00:33:31,750
Two orders of small Broccolino Basiliano.

919
00:33:32,550 --> 00:33:36,290
Eight pomegranate slushies.

920
00:33:36,520 --> 00:33:38,289
Three coffee slushies.

921
00:33:38,290 --> 00:33:40,160
And ten orders of tiramisu.

922
00:33:43,160 --> 00:33:44,229
What should we send out first?

923
00:33:44,230 --> 00:33:46,530
- We can do it, head chef.
- We can do this.

924
00:33:47,030 --> 00:33:48,030
(Order Status for the service team)

925
00:33:48,030 --> 00:33:49,030
(Tteokramisu chestnut, coffee slushy, pomegranate slushy)

926
00:33:49,031 --> 00:33:50,429
(8 dishes, 10 desserts, 11 drinks)

927
00:33:50,430 --> 00:33:51,670
(A total order of 29 items)

928
00:33:52,270 --> 00:33:54,340
(She tries to stay calm.)

929
00:33:54,370 --> 00:33:55,610
Hold on, what was it again?

930
00:33:56,240 --> 00:33:58,309
(Just then, more customers arrive.)

931
00:33:58,310 --> 00:34:00,339
Welcome. How many are you?

932
00:34:00,340 --> 00:34:02,950
Three more elementary school kids just came in.

933
00:34:03,080 --> 00:34:05,049
- What kind of customers?
- Elementary school kids...

934
00:34:05,050 --> 00:34:06,496
- Elementary school kids?
- as customers.

935
00:34:06,520 --> 00:34:08,249
One small original tteokbokki,

936
00:34:08,250 --> 00:34:10,049
one small ghost pepper tteokbokki,

937
00:34:10,050 --> 00:34:11,350
and two sodas.

938
00:34:12,020 --> 00:34:14,860
- Is that from another table?
- Yes, it is.

939
00:34:15,060 --> 00:34:16,289
(Tteokbokki Order Status)

940
00:34:16,290 --> 00:34:18,330
(Small original tteokbokki, small mala tteokbokki)

941
00:34:18,630 --> 00:34:20,529
(There are 6 orders of tteokbokki for the large group, )

942
00:34:20,530 --> 00:34:23,730
(but there are only 3 burners.)

943
00:34:23,970 --> 00:34:25,129
Here's my plan.

944
00:34:25,130 --> 00:34:27,740
(That's when Young Ji comes up with a brilliant idea.)

945
00:34:28,700 --> 00:34:30,510
We'll serve one small original tteokbokki,

946
00:34:31,440 --> 00:34:32,779
Broccolino Basiliano, and the challenge together.

947
00:34:32,780 --> 00:34:34,386
After that, we'll serve one original for the other table.

948
00:34:34,410 --> 00:34:37,280
(Jade Emperor, small Basiliano, small original tteokbokki)

949
00:34:37,680 --> 00:34:39,519
(Basiliano and Jade Emperor for the large group)

950
00:34:39,520 --> 00:34:41,840
(Small original tteokbokki for the elementary school kids)

951
00:34:42,120 --> 00:34:44,320
(She plans to make them at the same time.)

952
00:34:44,650 --> 00:34:46,260
Don't panic, Young Ji.

953
00:34:46,290 --> 00:34:47,659
- You can do it, chef.
- Young Ji, you can do it.

954
00:34:47,660 --> 00:34:49,089
Chef, you can do it.

955
00:34:49,090 --> 00:34:52,429
You're the one who just used all three burners at once.

956
00:34:52,430 --> 00:34:53,530
Yes, I can do this.

957
00:34:54,900 --> 00:34:58,330
(She turns on all three burners again.)

958
00:34:58,730 --> 00:35:02,210
(Dropping garaetteok into the original and basil tteokbokki)

959
00:35:02,510 --> 00:35:05,009
(Next up, it's Jade Emperor Tteokbokki.)

960
00:35:05,010 --> 00:35:07,610
(2 tablespoons of chili bean sauce)

961
00:35:07,810 --> 00:35:10,310
(1 teaspoon of ghost pepper powder)

962
00:35:10,610 --> 00:35:13,250
(3 tablespoons of Sichuan pepper oil)

963
00:35:13,650 --> 00:35:16,450
(Adding a 175cm-long whole garaetteok)

964
00:35:16,920 --> 00:35:19,120
(All she has to do is wait for the sauce to reduce.)

965
00:35:19,660 --> 00:35:21,119
Yu Jin, we have so many desserts to make.

966
00:35:21,120 --> 00:35:22,760
- One small tteokbokki.
- I know.

967
00:35:23,330 --> 00:35:25,166
- For the pomegranate slushy...
- There are ten tiramisus?

968
00:35:25,190 --> 00:35:26,329
How many pomegranate slushies are there?

969
00:35:26,330 --> 00:35:28,800
Five, six, seven, eight.

970
00:35:28,900 --> 00:35:30,220
- Are there ten tiramisus?
- Yes.

971
00:35:30,500 --> 00:35:32,140
- I'll start making the tiramisu.
- Okay.

972
00:35:32,170 --> 00:35:34,470
(She plans to make half of it in advance.)

973
00:35:34,800 --> 00:35:36,070
I'll take care of the drinks.

974
00:35:36,340 --> 00:35:38,300
- Thank you.
- Yu Jin, you take care of desserts.

975
00:35:38,370 --> 00:35:40,540
I can totally count on you, Eun Ji.

976
00:35:40,640 --> 00:35:41,880
We're one.

977
00:35:42,350 --> 00:35:43,379
We're definitely one.

978
00:35:43,380 --> 00:35:45,480
I'll start by serving the appetizers.

979
00:35:45,750 --> 00:35:47,450
(Serving the cream rice cakes first)

980
00:35:47,680 --> 00:35:49,989
At Space Rice Cake fine dining,

981
00:35:49,990 --> 00:35:52,489
we're developing a new menu item.

982
00:35:52,490 --> 00:35:55,159
I brought some in case you'd like to try it.

983
00:35:55,160 --> 00:35:57,060
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

984
00:35:57,190 --> 00:35:58,429
(Immediately after, )

985
00:35:58,430 --> 00:36:00,700
(she starts making slushies.)

986
00:36:01,030 --> 00:36:02,800
(One drink is ready.)

987
00:36:03,670 --> 00:36:06,399
(It's endless no matter how much she makes.)

988
00:36:06,400 --> 00:36:10,140
(The never-ending slushy cycle)

989
00:36:10,870 --> 00:36:14,140
(Serving while making it obvious that she's struggling)

990
00:36:14,340 --> 00:36:16,410
Stay in your seats. I got this.

991
00:36:16,580 --> 00:36:20,780
(Yu Jin is in charge of the tteokramisu chestnut.)

992
00:36:21,280 --> 00:36:23,489
(There's no end no matter how many she stacks up.)

993
00:36:23,490 --> 00:36:28,160
(The never-ending tteokramisu chestnut cycle)

994
00:36:28,720 --> 00:36:30,830
(Storing five of them in the fridge for now)

995
00:36:31,660 --> 00:36:33,699
If you don't mind,

996
00:36:33,700 --> 00:36:36,029
our pastry chef would like to hear...

997
00:36:36,030 --> 00:36:38,700
what you thought of the rice cakes.

998
00:36:39,040 --> 00:36:40,446
- They're delicious.
- The two of them tried.

999
00:36:40,470 --> 00:36:42,709
- Did you like them?
- Yes.

1000
00:36:42,710 --> 00:36:45,370
Do you think it would be better with more cream?

1001
00:36:45,540 --> 00:36:47,079
- The amount was perfect.
- It was perfect?

1002
00:36:47,080 --> 00:36:49,379
How was the amount of cream at that table?

1003
00:36:49,380 --> 00:36:50,949
- It was good enough.
- It was good enough?

1004
00:36:50,950 --> 00:36:53,320
- Okay. Thank you, everyone.
- Sure.

1005
00:36:54,350 --> 00:36:55,819
They said the cream rice cake was really delicious,

1006
00:36:55,820 --> 00:36:57,219
the amount of cream was just right,

1007
00:36:57,220 --> 00:36:59,190
and they liked how sweet the cream was.

1008
00:36:59,360 --> 00:37:00,590
Nice.

1009
00:37:02,360 --> 00:37:03,390
We should go for it.

1010
00:37:04,030 --> 00:37:05,830
Mi Hyun, let's make it an official menu item.

1011
00:37:06,130 --> 00:37:07,559
- Thank you.
- You're amazing.

1012
00:37:07,560 --> 00:37:09,030
(It passed the customer taste test.)

1013
00:37:09,400 --> 00:37:11,499
- Is it the challenge first?
- Yes, it is.

1014
00:37:11,500 --> 00:37:14,640
But the elementary school kids are waiting for the original tteokbokki.

1015
00:37:15,200 --> 00:37:17,140
I made their small original tteokbokki first.

1016
00:37:17,610 --> 00:37:19,539
I also prepared Broccolino Basiliano.

1017
00:37:19,540 --> 00:37:21,639
(What is she saying?)

1018
00:37:21,640 --> 00:37:22,710
It's okay.

1019
00:37:23,110 --> 00:37:24,849
I don't understand what you mean.

1020
00:37:24,850 --> 00:37:27,049
She made dishes for the reserved group and the other table.

1021
00:37:27,050 --> 00:37:28,520
- Is that what she means?
- Yes.

1022
00:37:28,650 --> 00:37:29,749
(Thinking)

1023
00:37:29,750 --> 00:37:32,360
Do you want me to stir-fry the beef loin?

1024
00:37:32,890 --> 00:37:34,889
- We're out of burners.
- Is that so?

1025
00:37:34,890 --> 00:37:36,850
Should I bring out the portable burner and do it?

1026
00:37:37,360 --> 00:37:38,429
That would be amazing.

1027
00:37:38,430 --> 00:37:40,750
I'll bring out the portable burner and cook the beef loin.

1028
00:37:41,760 --> 00:37:44,700
I was going to prep the beef loin, but we don’t have a burner.

1029
00:37:45,370 --> 00:37:46,500
Does anyone have one?

1030
00:37:46,600 --> 00:37:48,870
(It's complete chaos.)

1031
00:37:49,810 --> 00:37:51,969
If you cook all of that, Young Ji will use it.

1032
00:37:51,970 --> 00:37:53,939
- Okay.
- Thank you.

1033
00:37:53,940 --> 00:37:55,009
You're welcome.

1034
00:37:55,010 --> 00:37:56,810
(While Eun Ji is stir-frying the beef loin)

1035
00:37:57,380 --> 00:37:58,580
Small Basiliano is ready.

1036
00:37:59,220 --> 00:38:01,280
Who ordered the basil tteokbokki?

1037
00:38:01,950 --> 00:38:03,520
A small original tteokbokki is ready.

1038
00:38:03,790 --> 00:38:05,149
Make sure not to touch it.

1039
00:38:05,150 --> 00:38:06,590
(Serving the elementary school kids)

1040
00:38:06,790 --> 00:38:09,530
(And pollack roe and clam pasta is ready.)

1041
00:38:09,760 --> 00:38:11,089
- Be careful. It's hot.
- Okay.

1042
00:38:11,090 --> 00:38:12,190
(Serving the large group)

1043
00:38:12,400 --> 00:38:13,460
Enjoy your food.

1044
00:38:13,560 --> 00:38:15,159
- The challenge is ready.
- Okay.

1045
00:38:15,160 --> 00:38:16,346
(Enjoy your food until Jade Emperor Tteokbokki is served.)

1046
00:38:16,370 --> 00:38:18,270
- Ghost pepper tteokbokki is ready.
- Okay.

1047
00:38:18,370 --> 00:38:20,540
Young Ji, you can use all the fried food on the right.

1048
00:38:21,100 --> 00:38:22,369
- It's big today.
- Okay.

1049
00:38:22,370 --> 00:38:24,370
(Piling on a generous amount of fried toppings)

1050
00:38:24,740 --> 00:38:26,680
(And topping it off with beef loin)

1051
00:38:28,280 --> 00:38:30,360
(She sprinkles some Cheongyang chili pepper on top.)

1052
00:38:30,750 --> 00:38:31,950
(And...)

1053
00:38:32,620 --> 00:38:36,250
(squeezing in a generous amount of capsaicin sauce)

1054
00:38:38,050 --> 00:38:40,130
(It's a much more intense version of the challenge.)

1055
00:38:40,360 --> 00:38:42,789
- The challenge dish is ready.
- Could you put it up here?

1056
00:38:42,790 --> 00:38:44,459
- I'd appreciate it.
- It's terrifying today.

1057
00:38:44,460 --> 00:38:45,959
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1058
00:38:45,960 --> 00:38:47,760
- Warn them that it's very spicy.
- Nice.

1059
00:38:48,260 --> 00:38:50,029
The four of you...

1060
00:38:50,030 --> 00:38:52,200
taking on the Jade Emperor Tteokbokki challenge.

1061
00:38:52,600 --> 00:38:53,670
Please leave it here.

1062
00:38:54,870 --> 00:38:57,069
Head Chef Lee Young Ji came fully prepared...

1063
00:38:57,070 --> 00:39:00,010
- for today.
- That wasn't necessary.

1064
00:39:00,380 --> 00:39:01,380
(1 Jade Emperor Tteokbokki)

1065
00:39:01,381 --> 00:39:02,579
Thank you.

1066
00:39:02,580 --> 00:39:05,550
- Finish it with a sense of duty.
- Please take lots of fun photos.

1067
00:39:06,150 --> 00:39:07,426
Did the first group of customers fail?

1068
00:39:07,450 --> 00:39:08,519
- They made it.
- Did anyone make it?

1069
00:39:08,520 --> 00:39:10,020
- They made it?
- They made it?

1070
00:39:10,250 --> 00:39:11,850
Doesn't that mean that it's possible?

1071
00:39:12,150 --> 00:39:14,859
Our head chef was angry...

1072
00:39:14,860 --> 00:39:15,860
about their success.

1073
00:39:16,560 --> 00:39:19,429
So the difficulty level might have gone up...

1074
00:39:19,430 --> 00:39:21,160
- a little.
- This is going to kill us.

1075
00:39:21,600 --> 00:39:23,069
I'll be lenient since it's the first day.

1076
00:39:23,070 --> 00:39:25,129
(Version 1 for yesterday's challenge)

1077
00:39:25,130 --> 00:39:26,799
(Version 2 for today's challenge)

1078
00:39:26,800 --> 00:39:29,070
The food challenge gets spicier than before...

1079
00:39:29,370 --> 00:39:30,409
so that no one can succeed.

1080
00:39:30,410 --> 00:39:31,609
We'll start.

1081
00:39:31,610 --> 00:39:32,740
- Are you ready?
- Yes.

1082
00:39:33,410 --> 00:39:34,440
Ready, set, go.

1083
00:39:34,880 --> 00:39:35,950
You can do it.

1084
00:39:36,710 --> 00:39:37,809
(Bravely taking the first bite)

1085
00:39:37,810 --> 00:39:38,810
It looks spicy.

1086
00:39:39,180 --> 00:39:40,180
- Is it very spicy?
- Please enjoy.

1087
00:39:40,181 --> 00:39:41,619
Hang in there. You can do it.

1088
00:39:41,620 --> 00:39:43,689
- The flavor hits you at once.
- Hang in there.

1089
00:39:43,690 --> 00:39:45,249
- Is it like mala sauce?
- Yes.

1090
00:39:45,250 --> 00:39:48,159
- Does it taste like mala?
- Spicy mala can be very spicy.

1091
00:39:48,160 --> 00:39:50,830
(We thought that he was perfectly calm.)

1092
00:39:51,130 --> 00:39:52,189
Give me some tissue.

1093
00:39:52,190 --> 00:39:54,629
- Isn't it spicy? Don't you feel it?
- It's spicy.

1094
00:39:54,630 --> 00:39:57,130
(They can't think straight.)

1095
00:39:57,530 --> 00:39:59,770
Can you read the remaining orders for me?

1096
00:40:00,240 --> 00:40:02,370
Two medium original tteokbokki.

1097
00:40:02,510 --> 00:40:04,009
(1 medium mala tteokbokki, 1 small basil tteokbokki for the group)

1098
00:40:04,010 --> 00:40:06,250
(1 small mala tteokbokki for the elementary school kids)

1099
00:40:06,880 --> 00:40:07,910
Thank you.

1100
00:40:08,380 --> 00:40:09,509
Two small and three medium.

1101
00:40:09,510 --> 00:40:10,726
(Yu Jin goes to stir-fry the beef loin.)

1102
00:40:10,750 --> 00:40:12,980
- Is there any priority order?
- Did you say beef loin?

1103
00:40:13,380 --> 00:40:14,880
I'm stir-frying it now.

1104
00:40:15,420 --> 00:40:17,549
I meant priority order, not beef loin.

1105
00:40:17,550 --> 00:40:19,490
I'll take care of it.

1106
00:40:19,690 --> 00:40:21,170
- Thank you.
- Priority order? I see.

1107
00:40:21,520 --> 00:40:24,190
(Absolute chaos)

1108
00:40:24,360 --> 00:40:26,930
(Remaining Order Status)

1109
00:40:27,500 --> 00:40:30,900
(Meanwhile, Mimi makes another pollack roe and clam pasta.)

1110
00:40:31,400 --> 00:40:33,740
If the pasta is ready, may I decorate it and serve it?

1111
00:40:34,140 --> 00:40:36,110
(Finishing it up for the busy chef)

1112
00:40:36,240 --> 00:40:37,910
Here's one more dish for you.

1113
00:40:38,370 --> 00:40:40,110
It's hot. Hold it by the top.

1114
00:40:40,510 --> 00:40:42,439
Mimi, all your pasta orders are out.

1115
00:40:42,440 --> 00:40:43,649
I'm done.

1116
00:40:43,650 --> 00:40:44,650
(Mimi's orders are done.)

1117
00:40:44,880 --> 00:40:46,980
(And one person still has a long way to go.)

1118
00:40:47,150 --> 00:40:49,026
(Medium original, medium mala, small basil for the large group)

1119
00:40:49,050 --> 00:40:50,690
(There are rice cakes.)

1120
00:40:50,920 --> 00:40:52,680
(There are no rice cakes for the other two.)

1121
00:40:53,420 --> 00:40:54,990
(A long way off)

1122
00:40:55,560 --> 00:40:59,029
(Customers show up at the worst possible moment.)

1123
00:40:59,030 --> 00:41:00,760
Hello. Welcome.

1124
00:41:00,860 --> 00:41:02,029
- How many are you?
- We're two.

1125
00:41:02,030 --> 00:41:03,570
Two? Please go inside.

1126
00:41:04,030 --> 00:41:06,039
I'll put in the order. Thank you.

1127
00:41:06,040 --> 00:41:08,120
(Two friends' table: 1 small original tteokbokki...)

1128
00:41:08,200 --> 00:41:09,710
I'll read the order.

1129
00:41:10,010 --> 00:41:12,310
(Remaining Order Status)

1130
00:41:12,610 --> 00:41:15,139
- Small Broccolino is ready.
- Okay.

1131
00:41:15,140 --> 00:41:16,880
(Totally exhausted)

1132
00:41:18,010 --> 00:41:19,650
- It's been four minutes.
- Are you okay?

1133
00:41:19,820 --> 00:41:20,820
Do you want this?

1134
00:41:21,150 --> 00:41:24,120
- You can do it - You can do it.

1135
00:41:24,690 --> 00:41:27,090
(The kids start cheering them on.)

1136
00:41:27,420 --> 00:41:29,329
(The dads keep fighting their way through it.)

1137
00:41:29,330 --> 00:41:31,290
(The pot is starting to show the bottom.)

1138
00:41:31,630 --> 00:41:34,130
Success!

1139
00:41:34,830 --> 00:41:36,470
Did we get the wrong flavor or something?

1140
00:41:37,100 --> 00:41:39,130
- Was it not spicy?
- It was sweet.

1141
00:41:39,300 --> 00:41:40,370
It was sweet?

1142
00:41:40,500 --> 00:41:41,599
(He's just showing off.)

1143
00:41:41,600 --> 00:41:42,740
We'll test it.

1144
00:41:43,340 --> 00:41:45,209
Everyone, scream!

1145
00:41:45,210 --> 00:41:47,310
I think they completed the challenge.

1146
00:41:47,610 --> 00:41:48,839
- The challenge?
- The challenge?

1147
00:41:48,840 --> 00:41:50,809
(But it wasn't bad news only for Young Ji.)

1148
00:41:50,810 --> 00:41:52,279
Yes, they completed it successfully.

1149
00:41:52,280 --> 00:41:54,020
Where's my slushy? Is this it?

1150
00:41:54,650 --> 00:41:57,190
(They ran out of their slushies due to the challenge.)

1151
00:41:57,590 --> 00:41:59,990
Nine pomegranate slushies, please.

1152
00:42:00,090 --> 00:42:03,090
Nine on top of eight pomegranate slushies that you ordered?

1153
00:42:04,490 --> 00:42:05,660
I feel great.

1154
00:42:06,430 --> 00:42:09,429
- We met the Jade Emperor.
- That's why you crave some more.

1155
00:42:09,430 --> 00:42:10,430
(There isn't much left.)

1156
00:42:10,700 --> 00:42:12,570
(The slushy factory is back on.)

1157
00:42:13,070 --> 00:42:17,010
(She makes as many as possible.)

1158
00:42:18,640 --> 00:42:20,739
We're in trouble. We ran out of slushies.

1159
00:42:20,740 --> 00:42:22,809
I need to tell them...

1160
00:42:22,810 --> 00:42:25,180
that our pomegranate slushies are sold out.

1161
00:42:25,610 --> 00:42:29,250
Unfortunately, our pomegranate slushies are sold out.

1162
00:42:29,520 --> 00:42:31,389
- You should share them.
- I'll serve you only five.

1163
00:42:31,390 --> 00:42:34,189
- Okay. Thank you.
- I'm very sorry.

1164
00:42:34,190 --> 00:42:37,930
This isn't exactly fine dining, is it? I'm sorry, everyone.

1165
00:42:38,530 --> 00:42:40,929
Yu Jin, pomegranate slushies are sold out. Don't take more orders.

1166
00:42:40,930 --> 00:42:42,229
They're sold out for now.

1167
00:42:42,230 --> 00:42:44,046
- When they're ready...
- We'll sell them again.

1168
00:42:44,070 --> 00:42:45,700
(She runs to refill the slushy.)

1169
00:42:46,070 --> 00:42:48,040
- Medium original is ready.
- Okay.

1170
00:42:48,740 --> 00:42:51,270
(Frantically sending out dishes)

1171
00:42:51,570 --> 00:42:54,910
Original tteokbokki is your last one. Shall I serve on this side?

1172
00:42:55,210 --> 00:42:56,679
Is this our last dish?

1173
00:42:56,680 --> 00:42:58,609
Yes, and you have desserts coming up.

1174
00:42:58,610 --> 00:42:59,919
- By the way...
- That's right.

1175
00:42:59,920 --> 00:43:01,819
Earlier, you ordered ten.

1176
00:43:01,820 --> 00:43:04,649
How full are you now? If you're too full...

1177
00:43:04,650 --> 00:43:06,590
- I'm not full.
- You aren't?

1178
00:43:06,990 --> 00:43:08,920
(Of course not)

1179
00:43:09,220 --> 00:43:11,729
- Really? Shall I bring ten?
- Yes.

1180
00:43:11,730 --> 00:43:13,360
- Okay. Thank you.
- Thank you.

1181
00:43:14,060 --> 00:43:15,399
(Eun Ji will make tteokramisu chestnut.)

1182
00:43:15,400 --> 00:43:16,600
Tteokramisu chestnut!

1183
00:43:17,170 --> 00:43:19,100
Gosh, my back is killing me.

1184
00:43:19,640 --> 00:43:21,640
(Even though she's letting out groans of pain)

1185
00:43:23,240 --> 00:43:26,880
(She got the hang of piping the chestnut cream.)

1186
00:43:27,080 --> 00:43:29,550
This is insane. I'm getting so good at it.

1187
00:43:30,080 --> 00:43:32,080
(After all that intensive training)

1188
00:43:32,350 --> 00:43:34,320
(Plenty of them are ready to go.)

1189
00:43:34,780 --> 00:43:36,789
I'm getting better and better.

1190
00:43:36,790 --> 00:43:37,819
(A lot of self-praising)

1191
00:43:37,820 --> 00:43:40,489
- You're doing well.
- Be careful.

1192
00:43:40,490 --> 00:43:42,589
- Ten tteokramisu?
- Ten tteokramisu are coming out.

1193
00:43:42,590 --> 00:43:45,360
- Ten tteokramisu are coming out.
- That's amazing.

1194
00:43:46,360 --> 00:43:48,000
- Here are your desserts.
- They're here.

1195
00:43:49,530 --> 00:43:50,569
It's tteokramisu.

1196
00:43:50,570 --> 00:43:52,799
- It looks so good.
- Thank you.

1197
00:43:52,800 --> 00:43:54,940
- I'll serve you.
- Thank you so much.

1198
00:43:55,270 --> 00:43:57,170
Enjoy your dessert. Thank you.

1199
00:43:57,540 --> 00:44:00,610
(After overcoming the biggest hurdle)

1200
00:44:01,240 --> 00:44:02,379
Well done, everyone.

1201
00:44:02,380 --> 00:44:04,210
Serving ten tiramisus was impressive.

1202
00:44:04,750 --> 00:44:06,880
Yu Jin made them all in advance.

1203
00:44:07,480 --> 00:44:08,749
I love you.

1204
00:44:08,750 --> 00:44:09,889
I love you so much.

1205
00:44:09,890 --> 00:44:12,960
- I love you a lot today.
- I love you so much.

1206
00:44:14,120 --> 00:44:15,989
Small ghost pepper tteokbokki is ready.

1207
00:44:15,990 --> 00:44:17,089
Broccolino Basiliano is done.

1208
00:44:17,090 --> 00:44:18,959
- Yu Jin, small original is ready.
- Okay.

1209
00:44:18,960 --> 00:44:20,730
(Remaining Order Status)

1210
00:44:21,500 --> 00:44:23,269
(Mimi double-checks the orders for Young Ji.)

1211
00:44:23,270 --> 00:44:24,470
One small original tteokbokki.

1212
00:44:25,870 --> 00:44:28,470
There's still pollack roe and clam pasta.

1213
00:44:30,210 --> 00:44:31,940
Was there one pollack roe and clam pasta?

1214
00:44:32,240 --> 00:44:34,010
- Yes, at Table Four.
- Okay.

1215
00:44:34,410 --> 00:44:35,640
I must've missed it.

1216
00:44:36,410 --> 00:44:38,380
(When they were tackling the big group order)

1217
00:44:38,480 --> 00:44:40,080
I'll read the order.

1218
00:44:41,050 --> 00:44:42,550
Give it to me. Leave it there.

1219
00:44:43,420 --> 00:44:45,389
One small original tteokbokki.

1220
00:44:45,390 --> 00:44:47,259
One pollack roe and clam pasta.

1221
00:44:47,260 --> 00:44:48,759
- Black pepper?
- Yes, thank you.

1222
00:44:48,760 --> 00:44:49,790
Pomegranate slushies.

1223
00:44:50,190 --> 00:44:52,506
(She forgot about her own order while taking care of the head chef.)

1224
00:44:52,530 --> 00:44:53,729
(That was a close call.)

1225
00:44:53,730 --> 00:44:55,860
Gosh, I didn't hear anything.

1226
00:44:57,500 --> 00:44:59,440
I figured out the quickest way to make it.

1227
00:44:59,540 --> 00:45:01,040
- You can do it.
- I can do it.

1228
00:45:01,270 --> 00:45:02,630
(She jumps straight into cooking.)

1229
00:45:02,910 --> 00:45:05,240
(Drizzling in a generous amount of olive oil)

1230
00:45:05,470 --> 00:45:06,539
(Tossing in garlic and crushed red pepper)

1231
00:45:06,540 --> 00:45:07,840
It's nice and spicy.

1232
00:45:08,410 --> 00:45:10,780
(She smiles first even though she's in a hurry.)

1233
00:45:11,010 --> 00:45:12,450
(Your food will be ready soon.)

1234
00:45:15,680 --> 00:45:16,819
I feel like I'm not...

1235
00:45:16,820 --> 00:45:18,180
- in this world anymore.
- Me too.

1236
00:45:18,690 --> 00:45:19,690
Go.

1237
00:45:19,691 --> 00:45:21,490
(She uses the wok from out of this world.)

1238
00:45:21,860 --> 00:45:22,929
You're doing so well.

1239
00:45:22,930 --> 00:45:24,860
(Mimi's rock star cooking comes to an end.)

1240
00:45:25,360 --> 00:45:27,500
- Ta-da.
- It looks beautiful.

1241
00:45:27,730 --> 00:45:30,030
(We'll serve it right away.)

1242
00:45:30,770 --> 00:45:33,640
(The next customer toddles in.)

1243
00:45:33,700 --> 00:45:35,569
What's this?

1244
00:45:35,570 --> 00:45:37,069
- This is...
- Is that the menu?

1245
00:45:37,070 --> 00:45:38,070
So cute.

1246
00:45:38,610 --> 00:45:41,910
- Mommy, I want food.
- What shall we eat?

1247
00:45:43,080 --> 00:45:44,109
(Yu Jin goes to take the order.)

1248
00:45:44,110 --> 00:45:46,249
Would you like to order? Hello.

1249
00:45:46,250 --> 00:45:47,280
Hi.

1250
00:45:48,350 --> 00:45:51,149
- One tteokramisu chestnut...
- Yes.

1251
00:45:51,150 --> 00:45:54,990
- and that broccoli dish.
- Okay.

1252
00:45:55,860 --> 00:45:57,489
(As soon as she's done taking the orders, )

1253
00:45:57,490 --> 00:45:59,130
(a new group of customers enter.)

1254
00:45:59,260 --> 00:46:00,929
- Small.
- One small.

1255
00:46:00,930 --> 00:46:04,269
Basil... Broccolino Basiliano...

1256
00:46:04,270 --> 00:46:06,870
I'm asking just in case.

1257
