1665
00:59:42,720 --> 00:59:43,819
- The total sales?
- Yes.

1666
00:59:43,820 --> 00:59:45,589
- It's almost 1,000 dollars.
- It's 800 dollars.

1667
00:59:45,590 --> 00:59:46,619
(It's almost 1,000 dollars!)

1668
00:59:46,620 --> 00:59:48,289
(Card payment: 805.70 dollars, Cash payment: 57 dollars)

1669
00:59:48,290 --> 00:59:49,419
(Calculation mistake: 29.80 dollars)

1670
00:59:49,420 --> 00:59:50,589
(Total: 832.90 dollars)

1671
00:59:50,590 --> 00:59:51,990
(But...)

1672
00:59:52,160 --> 00:59:53,629
- I have a question.
- Yes.

1673
00:59:53,630 --> 00:59:56,799
The middle-aged man we hired for just a while.

1674
00:59:56,800 --> 00:59:58,299
What's his hourly wage?

1675
00:59:58,300 --> 01:00:00,230
- The minimum wage...
- Yes.

1676
01:00:00,800 --> 01:00:03,039
Is 10.32 dollars.

1677
01:00:03,040 --> 01:00:04,439
- He worked for 30 minutes.
- But...

1678
01:00:04,440 --> 01:00:06,439
- it was late.
- Like... Yes.

1679
01:00:06,440 --> 01:00:08,179
- He worked overtime.
- Overtime pay.

1680
01:00:08,180 --> 01:00:11,479
So it's supposed to be 16 dollars. How long did he work?

1681
01:00:11,480 --> 01:00:12,549
Hold on, 16 dollars is...

1682
01:00:12,550 --> 01:00:14,920
the price of one Don't Eat Ghost Pepper Tteokbokki.

1683
01:00:15,020 --> 01:00:17,119
Didn't you earn more than 800 dollars today?

1684
01:00:17,120 --> 01:00:19,150
But we...

1685
01:00:19,490 --> 01:00:20,919
But he was pretty efficient.

1686
01:00:20,920 --> 01:00:24,359
- He really was a big help.
- He was efficient.

1687
01:00:24,360 --> 01:00:26,059
As long as Yeong Seok doesn't get a lot.

1688
01:00:26,060 --> 01:00:27,799
Then if we maintain...

1689
01:00:27,800 --> 01:00:29,859
a good relationship with the middle-aged man,

1690
01:00:29,860 --> 01:00:31,429
pay him well and such.

1691
01:00:31,430 --> 01:00:33,499
- Can we work tomorrow too?
- Of course.

1692
01:00:33,500 --> 01:00:34,769
- Really?
- During busy hours.

1693
01:00:34,770 --> 01:00:35,969
(Negotiation complete)

1694
01:00:35,970 --> 01:00:38,940
(1 Yeong Seok equals 1 mala tteokbokki.)

1695
01:00:39,440 --> 01:00:42,109
When ten tteokramisu chestnuts were served,

1696
01:00:42,110 --> 01:00:44,580
- I felt ecstatic.
- I know what you mean.

1697
01:00:44,680 --> 01:00:47,579
I was so surprised with how fast Yu Jin was.

1698
01:00:47,580 --> 01:00:49,380
Young Ji got the hang of it too.

1699
01:00:49,520 --> 01:00:51,596
- A cash register would be nice.
- About 100 dollars.

1700
01:00:51,620 --> 01:00:53,720
So this was what happened.

1701
01:00:54,090 --> 01:00:55,289
I had to calculate...

1702
01:00:55,290 --> 01:00:56,890
for ten people.

1703
01:00:57,090 --> 01:00:59,089
My hands started to tremble.

1704
01:00:59,090 --> 01:01:00,829
- Of course.
- "How do I handle this?"

1705
01:01:00,830 --> 01:01:03,159
The bill was super long, like ten items on it.

1706
01:01:03,160 --> 01:01:05,370
I came halfway.

1707
01:01:05,530 --> 01:01:07,199
I was supposed to type 16 dollars,

1708
01:01:07,200 --> 01:01:09,100
but I typed 160 dollars instead.

1709
01:01:09,300 --> 01:01:10,739
She was like, "We'll do it."

1710
01:01:10,740 --> 01:01:12,909
So I was like, "It's okay. Wait, where was I calculating?"

1711
01:01:12,910 --> 01:01:14,079
Okay.

1712
01:01:14,080 --> 01:01:16,010
Everything else is fine, but a cash register.

1713
01:01:16,640 --> 01:01:18,449
We accept real money,

1714
01:01:18,450 --> 01:01:19,749
- so when you calculate it, - Exactly.

1715
01:01:19,750 --> 01:01:21,119
- you'll feel nervous.
- It's pressuring.

1716
01:01:21,120 --> 01:01:23,750
- It's so pressuring.
- They said they'd do it,

1717
01:01:24,220 --> 01:01:26,619
and I hate myself for thinking they might've calculated...

1718
01:01:26,620 --> 01:01:28,190
a bit less.

1719
01:01:28,560 --> 01:01:31,090
The customer who ate Jade Emperor Tteokbokki said,

1720
01:01:31,260 --> 01:01:32,430
"It's sweet."

1721
01:01:33,130 --> 01:01:34,330
She's insulted again.

1722
01:01:35,430 --> 01:01:37,899
Really? We keep giving away free 40-dollar dishes.

1723
01:01:37,900 --> 01:01:39,299
Exactly.

1724
01:01:39,300 --> 01:01:41,169
It's better than them feeling ill afterwards.

1725
01:01:41,170 --> 01:01:42,569
But we can take a one-day break.

1726
01:01:42,570 --> 01:01:44,109
Yes, we should.

1727
01:01:44,110 --> 01:01:46,339
I have a list of city tour...

1728
01:01:46,340 --> 01:01:48,239
