1738
01:02:08,300 --> 01:02:09,830
without a care in the world.

1739
01:02:10,900 --> 01:02:12,770
I'm thinking if I ever had that time.

1740
01:02:13,200 --> 01:02:14,439
(It feels like her previous life.)

1741
01:02:14,440 --> 01:02:16,670
I felt it as I was making tteokbokki.

1742
01:02:16,970 --> 01:02:19,039
"I think I've lived 20 years doing this."

1743
01:02:19,040 --> 01:02:21,280
I'm really curious about the general store.

1744
01:02:21,780 --> 01:02:23,539
- The general store.
- We didn't get to go.

1745
01:02:23,540 --> 01:02:25,410
It sounds like paradise.

1746
01:02:25,710 --> 01:02:27,920
(The rumored place of wonders)

1747
01:02:28,180 --> 01:02:29,579
"Have you been to paradise?"

1748
01:02:29,580 --> 01:02:31,020
"Have you seen the blue sky?"

1749
01:02:31,220 --> 01:02:32,589
"Have you seen the blue country?"

1750
01:02:32,590 --> 01:02:34,459
(Have you seen the blue sky)

1751
01:02:34,460 --> 01:02:36,059
- "Have you seen the blue country?"
- Mimi.

1752
01:02:36,060 --> 01:02:37,906
You always come back from the general store like this.

1753
01:02:37,930 --> 01:02:39,259
"You know, the general store has..."

1754
01:02:39,260 --> 01:02:41,430
"this and that."

1755
01:02:41,500 --> 01:02:43,000
All we do is...

1756
01:02:43,200 --> 01:02:44,530
(Exclaiming)

1757
01:02:44,570 --> 01:02:47,140
We went to the general store today...

1758
01:02:47,240 --> 01:02:49,039
You must check it out when the show airs.

1759
01:02:49,040 --> 01:02:50,909
All we could think about were you two.

1760
01:02:50,910 --> 01:02:52,569
"I'll buy the boots for Young Ji."

1761
01:02:52,570 --> 01:02:54,016
- "This is perfect for Mimi."
- I thought so too.

1762
01:02:54,040 --> 01:02:55,879
We did all sorts of things.

1763
01:02:55,880 --> 01:02:57,950
And just for buying one gimbap,

1764
01:02:58,150 --> 01:02:59,379
- I...
- I didn't expect...

1765
01:02:59,380 --> 01:03:01,120
- to be criticized so badly.
- One gimbap.

1766
01:03:01,420 --> 01:03:04,490
- I had a reason.
- I never imagined.

1767
01:03:04,820 --> 01:03:06,649
- But I understand why you did that.
- Right before you came,

1768
01:03:06,650 --> 01:03:08,766
Producer Ye Seul came to me, and with her signature tone said,

1769
01:03:08,790 --> 01:03:11,430
"Young Ji, I have something to tell you."

1770
01:03:11,960 --> 01:03:13,429
"How much did you sell yesterday?"

1771
01:03:13,430 --> 01:03:14,530
It was 400 dollars.

1772
01:03:14,800 --> 01:03:16,600
"They spent 300 dollars on grocery shopping."

1773
01:03:16,700 --> 01:03:18,176
- She provoked you.
- She provoked me.

1774
01:03:18,200 --> 01:03:19,599
We came right after that, didn't we?

1775
01:03:19,600 --> 01:03:21,239
You did, with gimbap.

1776
01:03:21,240 --> 01:03:22,299
It's her scheme.

1777
01:03:22,300 --> 01:03:23,699
- She provoked you on purpose.
- She did that on purpose.

1778
01:03:23,700 --> 01:03:24,709
You fell for it.

1779
01:03:24,710 --> 01:03:26,539
- You fell for it.
- I've been on many survival shows,

1780
01:03:26,540 --> 01:03:28,486
- but I failed to recognize it.
- You didn't know.

1781
01:03:28,510 --> 01:03:30,210
In the end, I ate most of the gimbap.

1782
01:03:30,650 --> 01:03:31,750
I'm so sorry.

1783
01:03:31,980 --> 01:03:34,119
You and Mimi kept refusing to eat,

1784
01:03:34,120 --> 01:03:35,779
saying you didn't have an appetite.

1785
01:03:35,780 --> 01:03:38,050
So I thought you should have a proper lunch at least.

1786
01:03:38,250 --> 01:03:40,789
We had a time limit,

1787
01:03:40,790 --> 01:03:42,319
but we ran and got it somehow.

1788
01:03:42,320 --> 01:03:44,629
We ran to buy that gimbap.

1789
01:03:44,630 --> 01:03:45,730
- You...
- Yes.

1790
01:03:46,360 --> 01:03:47,430
Hold on.

1791
01:03:48,500 --> 01:03:50,729
Are you serious? What's wrong with her?

1792
01:03:50,730 --> 01:03:52,030
(Fidgety)

1793
01:03:52,130 --> 01:03:53,650
- This is so funny.
- Was it that sad?

1794
01:03:53,770 --> 01:03:56,339
- Was it that sad?
- Are you two dating?

1795
01:03:56,340 --> 01:03:57,569
I'm sorry, Yu Jin.

1796
01:03:57,570 --> 01:03:58,909
I totally get it.

1797
01:03:58,910 --> 01:04:00,779
- If you watch what happened before.
- Were you that upset?

1798
01:04:00,780 --> 01:04:01,810
I wasn't upset.

1799
01:04:02,010 --> 01:04:03,340
It's not because of you.

1800
01:04:04,150 --> 01:04:06,709
She can't sleep at night if I leave it at this.

1801
01:04:06,710 --> 01:04:08,180
- It's not because of you.
- So...

1802
01:04:08,680 --> 01:04:10,549
I shed a tear...

1803
01:04:10,550 --> 01:04:12,519
- while laughing.
- Because it's funny.

1804
01:04:12,520 --> 01:04:14,260
I was so upset, but I held it in.

1805
01:04:14,360 --> 01:04:15,720
"She must be sensitive now."

1806
01:04:16,120 --> 01:04:17,189
(Holding back her tears)

1807
01:04:17,190 --> 01:04:19,229
I held it in and went to a corner.

1808
01:04:19,230 --> 01:04:21,159
During that time, I turned around like this...

1809
01:04:21,160 --> 01:04:22,430
to avoid the camera.

1810
01:04:24,300 --> 01:04:25,670
(She has nothing to say.)

1811
01:04:25,770 --> 01:04:27,600
(The story Young Ji didn't know)

1812
01:04:27,670 --> 01:04:30,669
- Is there anything you want to eat?
- What about you, Mimi?

1813
01:04:30,670 --> 01:04:32,469
- If you're hungry.
- Not really.

1814
01:04:32,470 --> 01:04:33,539
Okay.

1815
01:04:33,540 --> 01:04:35,909
- We'll just have the basil dish.
- Okay.

1816
01:04:35,910 --> 01:04:37,656
(Since this morning, the youngest one has been...)

1817
01:04:37,680 --> 01:04:40,380
- I should get them vitamins.
- Make them have some.

1818
01:04:40,880 --> 01:04:43,819
I should get Mimi chocolates today. Did she have any yesterday?

1819
01:04:43,820 --> 01:04:46,349
Mimi had some chocolates before she left for work today.

1820
01:04:46,350 --> 01:04:48,196
And I gave her a piece of chocolate I brought from the US.

1821
01:04:48,220 --> 01:04:50,019
Let's limit our spending today.

1822
01:04:50,020 --> 01:04:52,360
- We shouldn't hurt our sales.
- That's right.

1823
01:04:53,090 --> 01:04:54,529
(Because their sales were humble, )

1824
01:04:54,530 --> 01:04:56,259
- We didn't spend much today.
- Thank you.

1825
01:04:56,260 --> 01:04:57,270
(they didn't have money.)

1826
01:04:58,970 --> 01:05:01,369
Run, Eun Ji. We don't have time. Hop in.

1827
01:05:01,370 --> 01:05:03,670
(They didn't have much time either.)

1828
01:05:04,040 --> 01:05:06,940
- The kitchen team needs it.
- We should get what they need.

1829
01:05:07,840 --> 01:05:09,410
(She was determined to do so.)

1830
01:05:09,680 --> 01:05:11,950
(How much did you spend on groceries today?)

1831
01:05:12,080 --> 01:05:13,379
(We spent 13.5 dollars to buy gimbap.)

1832
01:05:13,380 --> 01:05:14,740
- we spent 13.5 dollars.
- Gimbap?

1833
01:05:15,020 --> 01:05:16,660
- We bought gimbap.
- It's for our lunch.

1834
01:05:17,080 --> 01:05:20,250
(Young Ji, who didn't know, was more worried about money.)

1835
01:05:20,390 --> 01:05:22,390
Didn't you say you'd ask before you buy something?

1836
01:05:22,660 --> 01:05:24,089
(Yu Jin was flustered.)

1837
01:05:24,090 --> 01:05:27,560
If you yell at me for spending 13.5 dollars for lunch...

1838
01:05:27,930 --> 01:05:30,969
(They were hurt, but they kept it to themselves.)

1839
01:05:30,970 --> 01:05:33,050
I'm not yelling at you. We didn't even set a budget.

1840
01:05:33,530 --> 01:05:36,800
Young Ji must've felt sorry. She approached me like this.

1841
01:05:37,270 --> 01:05:38,539
- She suddenly said, - Let's stop eating.

1842
01:05:38,540 --> 01:05:39,810
"Hey, let me see your notepad."

1843
01:05:42,510 --> 01:05:45,280
- It was out of the blue.
- Are you high school students?

1844
01:05:45,650 --> 01:05:47,779
- Are you?
- "Hey, let me see your notepad."

1845
01:05:47,780 --> 01:05:49,179
- How cute.
- It’s amazing...

1846
01:05:49,180 --> 01:05:50,579
how accurately she remembers it.

1847
01:05:50,580 --> 01:05:52,749
- It's like an all-boys high school.
- It gets funnier.

1848
01:05:52,750 --> 01:05:56,189
I realized that was her way of making amends.

1849
01:05:56,190 --> 01:05:58,860
While thinking it was funny, I went, "Here."

1850
01:05:59,530 --> 01:06:00,760
- Did you?
- And...

1851
01:06:01,130 --> 01:06:03,700
she flipped the pages and went, "Gosh."

1852
01:06:03,960 --> 01:06:05,800
"Let's have some gimbap."

1853
01:06:06,330 --> 01:06:08,969
"Hey, let's have some gimbap."

1854
01:06:08,970 --> 01:06:10,039
That's a strange way to make amends.

1855
01:06:10,040 --> 01:06:11,640
Hey. Are you two going out or what?

1856
01:06:12,070 --> 01:06:13,309
- She was embarrassed.
- Why do you eat...

1857
01:06:13,310 --> 01:06:14,540
with your head down?

1858
01:06:15,040 --> 01:06:16,940
Look up and eat.

1859
01:06:17,750 --> 01:06:20,150
Why do you eat chicken with your head down?

1860
01:06:20,480 --> 01:06:21,480
Are you ashamed right now?

1861
01:06:21,481 --> 01:06:22,980
Hey, hold on. It's because...

1862
01:06:23,480 --> 01:06:25,390
I feel like this part will be aired.

1863
01:06:25,550 --> 01:06:26,589
(Correct.)

1864
01:06:26,590 --> 01:06:27,590
Keep going.

1865
01:06:28,190 --> 01:06:31,229
- You have your side of the story.
- Keep going.

1866
01:06:31,230 --> 01:06:33,511
- I'll let you tell it later.
- I don't have much to say.

1867
01:06:34,160 --> 01:06:35,299
"Hey, let's have some gimbap."

1868
01:06:35,300 --> 01:06:37,430
She said that, and I followed her.

1869
01:06:37,770 --> 01:06:40,099
While eating gimbap, I got over it already.

1870
01:06:40,100 --> 01:06:43,240
It wasn't worth getting upset about. While eating gimbap, I said,

1871
01:06:43,340 --> 01:06:44,969
"Yes, Young Ji. I'm glad you're enjoying gimbap."

1872
01:06:44,970 --> 01:06:46,569
"Have some more." And I wasn't upset anymore.

1873
01:06:46,570 --> 01:06:47,710
Do you know what's funny?

1874
01:06:48,110 --> 01:06:50,880
I was pissed at one point because I was anxious.

1875
01:06:51,350 --> 01:06:52,649
Maybe I really thought we could make 100,000 dollars.

1876
01:06:52,650 --> 01:06:53,910
So, I was anxious.

1877
01:06:54,010 --> 01:06:55,349
Then I had these flashbacks.

1878
01:06:55,350 --> 01:06:58,489
Come to think of it, Yu Jin bought a squishy toy, yogurt,

1879
01:06:58,490 --> 01:07:00,919
and snacks yesterday. I remembered them all.

1880
01:07:00,920 --> 01:07:02,420
I thought, "She wasted money."

1881
01:07:02,720 --> 01:07:05,030
The moment I lashed out, I had another flashback.

1882
01:07:05,390 --> 01:07:06,560
What was the flashback about?

1883
01:07:06,960 --> 01:07:09,100
Yu Jin punching numbers into a calculator...

1884
01:07:09,200 --> 01:07:10,930
to buy stuff with a discount.

1885
01:07:11,330 --> 01:07:14,140
- I was really worried about her.
- Okay.

1886
01:07:14,370 --> 01:07:17,100
She was anxious even before we left.

1887
01:07:17,410 --> 01:07:21,009
I've never seen her this anxious in person.

1888
01:07:21,010 --> 01:07:22,079
- Right.
- So,

1889
01:07:22,080 --> 01:07:24,579
like her manager,

1890
01:07:24,580 --> 01:07:27,520
- I wanted to take good care of her.
- That's right.

1891
01:07:27,850 --> 01:07:29,349
While talking about the flashback,

1892
01:07:29,350 --> 01:07:31,150
I remembered how I was, and I was suddenly...

1893
01:07:31,420 --> 01:07:32,589
(Choked up)

1894
01:07:32,590 --> 01:07:34,820
I thought, "Yes, I cared about her to this extent."

1895
01:07:35,520 --> 01:07:36,890
I had flashbacks.

1896
01:07:37,220 --> 01:07:39,130
(She has nothing to say.)

1897
01:07:39,560 --> 01:07:42,029
That was before. I'm not upset at all now.

1898
01:07:42,030 --> 01:07:43,729
- You don't feel upset.
- We made amends.

1899
01:07:43,730 --> 01:07:45,869
- I understand her completely.
- Sit straight.

1900
01:07:45,870 --> 01:07:47,740
I was very surprised just now.

1901
01:07:48,140 --> 01:07:49,640
She loves me a lot.

1902
01:07:50,440 --> 01:07:53,470
- What's with you?
- It's a kind of agape love.

1903
01:07:53,770 --> 01:07:56,409
- It's not. Don't take it too far.
- Is that so?

1904
01:07:56,410 --> 01:07:59,009
I'm really concerned about you. And I keep thinking about you.

1905
01:07:59,010 --> 01:08:01,549
- It's ape love...
- What's agape love?

1906
01:08:01,550 --> 01:08:04,190
- What's agape love?
- I don't really know.

1907
01:08:05,450 --> 01:08:08,120
- Why did you pretend to know it?
- It's because...

1908
01:08:08,220 --> 01:08:11,429
Yu Jin didn't love me this much during Season 1 and 2.

1909
01:08:11,430 --> 01:08:14,129
But I could suddenly feel how deeply she cared for me.

1910
01:08:14,130 --> 01:08:15,629
I felt like I'm So Ji Sub...

1911
01:08:15,630 --> 01:08:17,099
- from "I'm Sorry, I Love You."
- Like Moo Hyeok?

1912
01:08:17,100 --> 01:08:18,499
And she's Song Eun Chae.

1913
01:08:18,500 --> 01:08:21,100
When I saw her cry, she resembled Eun Chae a bit.

1914
01:08:21,570 --> 01:08:22,700
Gosh.

1915
01:08:22,900 --> 01:08:25,739
- Stop shooting a drama.
- We're done.

1916
01:08:25,740 --> 01:08:27,239
Hey, doesn't it feel great...

1917
01:08:27,240 --> 01:08:28,800
- to have sweats after work?
- It does.

1918
01:08:29,580 --> 01:08:31,609
- I'll have my favorite ice cream.
- Me too.

1919
01:08:31,610 --> 01:08:33,090
- I love it.
- Is this your favorite?

1920
01:08:33,210 --> 01:08:34,619
- Nice.
- This is the original one.

1921
01:08:34,620 --> 01:08:36,796
- The original one is delicious too.
- I'll have the corn flavor.

1922
01:08:36,820 --> 01:08:38,149
I got the new flavor.

1923
01:08:38,150 --> 01:08:41,159
- I got salted milk and caramel.
- It's salted milk and caramel.

1924
01:08:41,160 --> 01:08:42,960
- Thank you.
- It looks good.

1925
01:08:46,390 --> 01:08:47,599
This is...

1926
01:08:47,600 --> 01:08:48,629
(Savoring)

1927
01:08:48,630 --> 01:08:50,560
It's salted milk ice cream with caramel.

1928
01:08:51,130 --> 01:08:52,890
- You'd love it, Mimi.
- It must be so soft.

1929
01:08:53,030 --> 01:08:54,340
Try it. It's really good.

1930
01:08:54,640 --> 01:08:56,700
- It's something you'd love.
- It's so tasty.

1931
01:08:56,970 --> 01:08:58,040
(Amazed)

1932
01:08:58,310 --> 01:08:59,670
- Is it good?
- It's good. Try it.

1933
01:08:59,910 --> 01:09:02,679
Sticky rice cake goes well with ice cream.

1934
01:09:02,680 --> 01:09:04,309
- It's good.
- It's really tasty, Eun Ji.

1935
01:09:04,310 --> 01:09:07,049
- We can make a dessert like this.
- Sounds good.

1936
01:09:07,050 --> 01:09:08,519
- It's so good.
- I like the idea.

1937
01:09:08,520 --> 01:09:09,550
Let's copy it.

1938
01:09:10,680 --> 01:09:12,789
Don't you think the rice cake has gotten softer?

1939
01:09:12,790 --> 01:09:15,090
Everyone loves this one. You can't go wrong with this.

1940
01:09:15,390 --> 01:09:18,759
Can't we develop a new menu...

1941
01:09:18,760 --> 01:09:20,930
by putting ice cream and rice cake together?

1942
01:09:21,360 --> 01:09:23,429
- Sounds good.
- Yes. I think it's a good idea.

1943
01:09:23,430 --> 01:09:24,430
I love it.

1944
01:09:24,670 --> 01:09:26,930
(At their accommodations after work)

1945
01:09:27,230 --> 01:09:28,399
(Beeping)

1946
01:09:28,400 --> 01:09:29,400
Someone's here.

1947
01:09:30,070 --> 01:09:31,270
Who is it?

1948
01:09:31,840 --> 01:09:33,939
- An intruder.
- An intruder.

1949
01:09:33,940 --> 01:09:35,509
You got ready for bed real fast.

1950
01:09:35,510 --> 01:09:37,210
- We were just chatting?
- Really?

1951
01:09:37,440 --> 01:09:40,350
I'm here to borrow your foam roller.

1952
01:09:40,450 --> 01:09:43,249
We talked about this earlier, but Eun Ji and I...

1953
01:09:43,250 --> 01:09:44,750
(Chit-chatting while she's here)

1954
01:09:44,990 --> 01:09:47,520
- It's hard to jot down the orders.
- It is.

1955
01:09:48,590 --> 01:09:49,619
It's so hard.

1956
01:09:49,620 --> 01:09:51,990
The names are like Don't Eat Ghost Pepper Tteokbokki...

1957
01:09:52,560 --> 01:09:54,829
- I tried to shorten it.
- Okay.

1958
01:09:54,830 --> 01:09:57,059
Without talking to everyone beforehand,

1959
01:09:57,060 --> 01:10:00,129
I just wrote "Mala," and it created confusion.

1960
01:10:00,130 --> 01:10:01,400
So before we start tomorrow,

1961
01:10:02,000 --> 01:10:04,709
we should figure out ways to simplify the dish names.

1962
01:10:04,710 --> 01:10:05,769
(The sales talk continues even after work.)

1963
01:10:05,770 --> 01:10:08,440
- That would be great.
- The best way is...

1964
01:10:09,380 --> 01:10:12,549
It should be easy to hear for Young Ji.

1965
01:10:12,550 --> 01:10:15,319
It's simple for me because it's pollack roe and clams.

1966
01:10:15,320 --> 01:10:17,050
- You can call it whatever.
- Yes.

1967
01:10:17,420 --> 01:10:19,720
For Young Ji, let's go with the original,

1968
01:10:20,320 --> 01:10:21,360
the mala,

1969
01:10:21,560 --> 01:10:23,089
- And basil.
- and the basil.

1970
01:10:23,090 --> 01:10:24,630
If you keep it simple like that,

1971
01:10:24,730 --> 01:10:26,230
it would be the best.

1972
01:10:26,430 --> 01:10:27,999
And it's easier for us too.

1973
01:10:28,000 --> 01:10:30,799
- It's easier to write and read.
- It's easier to write down.

1974
01:10:30,800 --> 01:10:34,639
You wrote the whole name for the ghost pepper tteokbokki.

1975
01:10:34,640 --> 01:10:37,040
And that one and broccoli are confusing too.

1976
01:10:37,170 --> 01:10:39,569
Exactly. You wrote the whole name down.

1977
01:10:39,570 --> 01:10:41,279
- But...
- You wrote down broccoli too.

1978
01:10:41,280 --> 01:10:44,080
But when we shortened it and didn't write the whole name,

1979
01:10:44,410 --> 01:10:46,549
- since we scribbled, - It's confusing.

1980
01:10:46,550 --> 01:10:48,750
The names were confusing.

1981
01:10:49,580 --> 01:10:52,289
- You're here.
- What is this?

1982
01:10:52,290 --> 01:10:54,559
(Young Ji joins them.)

1983
01:10:54,560 --> 01:10:57,259
- You didn't take a shower.
- No.

1984
01:10:57,260 --> 01:10:59,090
- You didn't take a shower?
- No.

1985
01:10:59,530 --> 01:11:02,199
- No. I'm going to wash up now.
- What did you do, then?

1986
01:11:02,200 --> 01:11:03,999
- I was taking it easy.
- You watched something, right?

1987
01:11:04,000 --> 01:11:05,570
Take a shower first, Young Ji.

1988
01:11:05,870 --> 01:11:09,400
Let's keep the names as Basil and Mala between us.

1989
01:11:09,940 --> 01:11:12,270
- That sounds great.
- On the order sheets.

1990
01:11:12,470 --> 01:11:15,479
- We should say Basil and Mala.
- Yes. We'll do that tomorrow.

1991
01:11:15,480 --> 01:11:17,510
(They agreed to shorten the names.)

1992
01:11:18,510 --> 01:11:21,080
(The 2nd day of business drew to a close.)

1993
01:11:22,720 --> 01:11:26,350
(Morning has come to Space Rice Cake.)

1994
01:11:26,950 --> 01:11:29,660
- Hello.
- Good morning.

1995
01:11:29,990 --> 01:11:31,930
- Hello.
- Good morning.

1996
01:11:33,330 --> 01:11:35,330
- Chang Dae.
- Actually, it isn't a good morning.

1997
01:11:35,430 --> 01:11:36,729
My whole body is sore.

1998
01:11:36,730 --> 01:11:38,176
(Going to work with her eyes half-closed)

1999
01:11:38,200 --> 01:11:39,670
One, two, three.

2000
01:11:39,730 --> 01:11:40,829
(First up in the morning)

2001
01:11:40,830 --> 01:11:41,939
Be careful.

2002
01:11:41,940 --> 01:11:42,940
(Putting out the sign)

2003
01:11:43,500 --> 01:11:44,540
Good.

2004
01:11:47,540 --> 01:11:48,880
Gosh. My lower back.

2005
01:11:49,640 --> 01:11:52,350
- Goodness. I like these.
- Gosh. What are these?

2006
01:11:52,980 --> 01:11:55,449
- It only has egg whites.
- I love egg whites.

2007
01:11:55,450 --> 01:11:56,780
I love egg whites too.

2008
01:11:57,380 --> 01:11:59,120
Gosh. It has cheese in it.

2009
01:11:59,750 --> 01:12:03,090
I like egg whites because yolks are high in cholesterol.

2010
01:12:03,420 --> 01:12:06,130
- It's good to work at a restaurant.
- We have everything.

2011
01:12:06,490 --> 01:12:08,130
Do you want some super spicy sauce?

2012
01:12:08,760 --> 01:12:12,169
Hey, since it's easy to eat, we can take some on our way to work.

2013
01:12:12,170 --> 01:12:13,529
- Yes.
- I think I can eat 80 of these.

2014
01:12:13,530 --> 01:12:14,640
(Satisfied)

2015
01:12:14,900 --> 01:12:17,710
